Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 35 CLINICAL DATA  88 year old female with a fungating left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  FRAGMENTS OF SKIN AND SUBCUTANEOUS TISSUE WITH INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  CONSISTENT WITH DUCTAL TYPE  THE TUMOR EXTENDS TO MULTIPLE RESECTION MARGINS  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 12                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 50 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled with the patient s name and unit number only  are two pieces of tan pink to tan red soft tissue each partially covered by a tan pink epithelium  The first measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  the second measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  The larger piece is submitted in A  the smaller piece in B  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Joseph Vincent Bonventre  M D  David M Rudnick  M D  Katherine Keeley  M D  Peter Hedberg  M D  PART   BREAST MASS  LEFT   report_end , 1.
