Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  NUCCI  MARISA  ROSE  M D  DIAGNOSIS  by NUCCI MARISA ROSE M D  LEFT BREAST  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS  Atypical lobular hyperplasia  Fibrocystic changes with microcysts and apocrine metaplasia  Microcalcifications associated with benign epithelium  NOTE  Both areas of calcifications seen on specimen mammography were extensively sampled for histologic evaluation  CLINICAL DATA  History 61 year old woman S P right BCT REMOVED_DATE for treatment of stage I REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc No MX REMOVED_DATE cm  ILC with 11 negative lymph nodes  REMOVED_DATE  mammogram demonstrated 2 clusters of microcalcifications in the left breast  upper outer quadrant  Operation  Left breast wire double localization partial mastectomy  Clinical Diagnosis  Left breast microcalcifications  TISSUE SUBMITTED  Left breast  double wire localization partial mastectomy    inking per pathology protocol to mammo   Mammography  calcifications are seen in specimen  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by BRENN THOMAS M D  PH D  The specimen is received fresh  in one  1  part  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  double wire localization  partial mastectomy   and is inked the surgeon  The specimen is inked for the evaluation of margins  posterior   black  anterior   blue  superior   red  inferior   green  lateral   yellow  medial   orange  Sections of margins are submitted for microscopic examination  The specimen consists of a partial mastectomy specimen measuring 8 cm superior to inferior  7 cm medial to lateral  and 1 cm anterior to posterior  The specimen is placed on a radiogram grid  and the clusters of microcalcifications are identified according to the mammogram  The first cluster of microcalcifications is located just inferior of the superior margin  the second cluster of microcalcifications is located centrally in the specimen  The specimen consists of fibroadipose tissue with approximately 50  yellow adipose tissue and 50  white tan dense fibrous tissue  No circumcribed lesions are identified  The areas around the clusters of microcalcifications are extensively sampled and representative sections of all margins are submitted  Micro REMOVED_DATE  superior sections with first cluster of microcalcifications  multiple frags  RSS  Micro REMOVED_DATE  area between clusters of microcalcifications  4 frags  RSS  Micro REMOVED_DATE  area of second cluster of microcalcifications  multiple frags  Micro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin to cluster one and two of microcalcifications  multiple frags  RSS  Micro REMOVED_DATE  inferior margins  NOTE  NO MICRO  4 DICTATED  Reports to  KAELIN  CAROLYN  MARY M D  SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS  report_end , 0.
