Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Specimen Type  Breast  excisional tissue Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  JAMES D IGLEHART M D  CASE  BS 07 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PATIENT  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME Resident  Juan Miguel Mosquera  M D   M S C  Pathologist  Susan Lester  M D   Ph D  PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  BIOPSY FOR A PALPABLE MASS  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  consisting of cells with enlarged pleomorphic nuclei in a pagetoid pattern  best seen in block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  levels examined   There are very focal areas with a cribriform pattern  Immunoperoxidase studies were performed with the following results for the atypical cells  Estrogen receptor POSITIVE Progesterone receptor POSITIVE HER 2 neu HETEROGENEOUS  1  to focal 2   E Cadherin  POSITIVE Gynecomastia  Note  The patient had a prior core needle biopsy that showed epithelial hyperplasia with atypical features  reviewed as BWH REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The excision shows similar findings  The positivity for e cadherin excludes classification as lobular neoplasia  The findings are unusual in a male and would be best classified as atypical ductal hyperplasia  The entire specimen  including margins  is examined microscopically  This case was also reviewed by Dr  Andrea Richardson  who concurs with this interpretation  CLINICAL DATA  History  Core biopsy of the breast showed  hyperplasia with atypical features   History of malignant melanoma of the left thigh in 1994  Operation  Left breast mass  left breast biopsy  Operative Findings  None given  Clinical Diagnosis  Left breast mass  TISSUE SUBMITTED  A 1  Left breast mass  GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received in formalin  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   and consists of an unoriented yellow tan white  focally cauterized to hemorrhagic portion of fibroadipose tissue  1 9 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2 cm   Specimen is inked and serially sectioned  exhibiting a predominantly white tan  focally cystic fibrous stroma admixed with scant adipose tissue  No other gross lesions identified  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast tissue  multi frags  ESS  dfi lp CASE NUMBER  REMOVED_CASE_ID  By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated  of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es  related thereto  Final Diagnosis by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on 5 24 2007  report_end , 0.
