Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  09 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 08 CLINICAL DATA  Ultrasound core biopsy  Fibroadenoma vs phyllodes vs cancer  Left breast 7 o clock mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  7 O CLOCK   CORE BIOPSIES  ATYPICAL SPINDLE CELL PROLIFERATION   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The core biopsies demonstrate an atypical spindle cell proliferation  The spindle cells display mild nuclear pleomorphism  Mitotic figures are not appreciated  An epithelial component is not seen within the spindle cell proliferation and in areas the spindle cell proliferation appears to have a well defined border  The differential diagnosis includes an unusual form of PASH  fibromatosis  a fibroma or a phyllodes tumor  Excisional biopsy is needed to more accurately classify this lesion  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 19                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin  labeled with the patient s name  unit number and no designation as to site  are four cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm which are submitted in toto as cassette A  Gross Description by  JULIE ZWIRBLE Resident  AQING   AHCHEAN   CHEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  7 O CLOCK   CORE BIOPSIES, 0.
