Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY W REGIONAL LYMPH NODES Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  CIBAS  EDMUND  SAULIUS  M D  DIAGNOSIS  by CIBAS EDMUND SAULIUS M D   1  LEFT BREAST  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  Fat necrosis  fibrosis  chronic inflammation  and giant cell reaction  consistent with healing biopsy site  No residual tumor is identified  Fibrocystic changes  predominantly fibrosis   2  SKIN AND ADIPOSE TISSUE  Skin and subcutaneous fat with no significant pathologic change   3  MUSCLE  Skeletal muscle with no significant pathologic change  CLINICAL DATA  History  40 year old white woman with breast biopsy that showed intraductal and infiltrating carcinoma on REMOVED_DATE at BWH  Lumpectomy on REMOVED_DATE showed more tumor near margin  Now for complete mastectomy and reconstruction  Operation  Left simple mastectomy  Clinical Diagnosis  Left breast carcinoma  TISSUE SUBMITTED   1  Left breast   2  Skin and adipose tissue   3  Muscle  rectus abdomenus  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by NEISH ANDREW SCOTT M D  The specimen was received fresh  in a container bearing the patient s name and labelled  left breast   This specimen consists of a left simple mastectomy specimen measuring 21 x 19 x 5 cm and weighing 578 grams  A well defined axillary tail is not present on the specimen  Applied to the specimen is an ellipse of tan white skin measuring 8 x REMOVED_DATE cm  with an areola mearuring REMOVED_DATE  cm and a nipple measuring REMOVED_DATE cm  Inferior to the nipple is a well healed incision measuring 6 cm  Sectioning of the breast reveals largely fibrous  white  rubbery glistening breast parenchyma  Immediately deep to the healed biopsy incision is a focal area of firm granularity  surrounded by yellow opaque fat necrosis  This area does not form a discrete biopsy cavity  Micros  1 3  Deep resection margin underlying scar  3 frags  3 cass  RSs  Micros  4 8  Sections of breast beneath scar  5 frags  5 cass  RSS  Micro  9  Medial upper quadrant  1 frag  1 cass  RSS  Micro  10  Lower medial quadrant  1 frag  1 cass  RSS  Micro  11  Upper lateral quadrant  RSS  1 frag  1 cass  Micro  12  Lower lateral quadrant  1 frag  1 cass  RSS  Micro  13  Nipple  1 frag  1 cass  RSS  The second specimen  received fresh  in a container  bearing the patient s name and labelled  skin and adipose tissue   consists of a mass of fragmented adipose tissue measuring 13 x 11 x REMOVED_DATE cm  one fragment of adipose tissue has a triangular fragment of pink tan white skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  Micro  14  Skin and fat  1 frag  1 cass  RSS  The third specimen  received fresh in a container  bearing the patient s name and labelled  rectus abdomenus   consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of brown muscle  Micro  15  Muscle  1 frag  1 cass  ESS  NOTE  Sterile fragments of skin  fat  muscle are given to Dr  Sunday s lab for research purposes  Reports to  ERIKSSON  ELOF M D  SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST MASTECTOMY W REGIONAL LYMPH NODES  report_end , 0.
