Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  BOROWSKY  ALEXANDER  D   M D  DIAGNOSIS  by BOROWSKY ALEXANDER D  M D  1  RIGHT BREAST TISSUE  WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS   1  CARCINOMA IN SITU  See Note  Calcifications are present associated with both benign epithelium and areas of intraductal carcinoma  Atypical lobular hyperplasia  2  RIGHT BREAST TISSUE  WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIIONS   2  CARCINOMA IN SITU  See Note  Calcifications are present associated with both benign epithelium and areas of intraductal carcinoma  Atypical lobular hyperplasia  Skeletal muscle present  Columnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions  NOTE  In summary  this lesion has a somewhat uncertain capacity  and may be a marker for an increased local risk of invasive carcinoma  like a ductal carcinoma in situ lesion  in addition to the generalized  bilateral  risk implied by lobular carcinoma in situ  In the setting of a strong family history of breast or ovarian carcinoma  it might bre reasonable to expect precancerous intraductal lesions to arise multifocally  This case was reviewed by Dr  Lester  CLINICAL DATA  History  LCIS oif upper outer quadrant of right breast  with pagetoid extension into ducts  Calcifications were associated with benign breast tissue  and rarely with the LCIS  Now new calcifications in RUOQ Operation  Right needle localization biopsy  Clinical Diagnosis  Calcifications  TISSUE SUBMITTED   1  Right breast tissue  twisted wire marks caudate  2  Right breast tissue  Radiology  Specimen  1    calcification present  Specimen  2    calcification present  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by WOLGAMOT GREGORY M  M D  PH D  The specimen is received fresh  in two  2  parts  each labeled with the patient s name and unit number  Part  1    1  right breast tissue  twisted wire margin   consists of a single fragment of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue measuring 4 x 3 x REMOVED_DATE cm  There is a wire within the specimen and a portion of the wire is twisted  The specimen is inked in two colors  superior red and inferior green  Received with the specimen is a radiograph of the excised tissue with wire  The tissue around the wire is entirely submitted for histologic examination  On sectioning  no area suspicious for invasive carcinoma is identified  Micro REMOVED_DATE  tissue around wire  1 frag each  ESS  Micro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen  multiple frags  ESS  Part  2    2  right breast tissue   consists of two  2  fragments of tan white fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  and REMOVED_DATE x 3 x REMOVED_DATE cm  The larger fragment has a wire in place  Received with the specimen is a radiidgraph showing calcifications  There is no orientation to the specimen  The entire specimens are inked in black  The entire specimen is submitted for histologic examination  Micro REMOVED_DATE  tissue around wire  1 frag each  ESS  Micro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of larger fragment  multiple frags  ESS  Micro REMOVED_DATE  smaller fragment  multiple frags  ESS  Reports to  CHRISTIAN  ROGER  L  M D  SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS  report_end , 1.
Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT   BREAST Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  LESTER  SUSAN  M D  PH D  DIAGNOSIS  by LESTER SUSAN M D  PH D  CONSULT SLIDES FROM MERCY HOSPITAL  SPRINGFIELD  MA  RIGHT BREAST  CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A PALPABLE MASS  MHS 02 7451  REMOVED_DATE    Multiple cores of tissue with fibroadipose tissue  No breast epithelium is present  Note  There are two minute fragments of tissue  0 2 and REMOVED_DATE cm in size  present only on one of four slides from levels of the tissue block  level 3   These fragments are not present on the previous level  or on the subsequent level  On level 3  there are two duplicated sections of the tissue  Each of the fragments with carcinoma is present only on one of the two duplicated sections  One fragment consists of ductal carcinoma in situ  cribriform type  low nuclear grade  without necrosis and calcifications  associated with an area of microinvasion    REMOVED_DATE cm   The other fragment has a small focus of invasive carcinoma    REMOVED_DATE cm   The presence of carcinoma only in two minute tissue fragments present only once in multiple levels of the tissue is most consistent with artifactual introduction of these fragments during tissue processing  The absence of carcinoma in the subsequent excision  see below  supports this interpretation  Tissue typing could potentially be used to definitively identify the origin of this tissue  This case was reviewed at the Staff Pathology Conference with consensus that these fragments were most likely artifacts  No information is provided concerning the nature of the lesion biopsied  Although the findings could be consistent with a lipoma  the features are not specific  see note below   RIGHT BREAST  TWO EXCISIONS  MHS 02 7647  REMOVED_DATE    EXCISION  Biopsy site changes  see note   Lactational change in lobules  NOTE  The specimen was completely examined microscopically  Much of this biopsy and the second biopsy  see below  consists of adipose tissue  Although these findings could possibly be consistent with a lipoma  the findings are nonspecific  Clinical correlation will be necessary to determine the nature of the clinical lesion and whether or not these excisions include this lesion  No carcinoma or atypia is seen  SUPERIOR  Biopsy site changes  Lactational change in lobules  NOTE  The specimen was completely examined microscopically  SURGICAL ADDENDUM  by LESTER SUSAN M D  PH D  The case numbered  MHS 02 7451  was reviewed by Dr  Stuart Schnitt  Beth Israel Hospital  their number REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE   and the following is his consultation diagnosis  RIGHT BREAST  CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES  Fragments of adipose tissue with recent hemorrhage  see note  NOTE  One tissue profile on 1 slide  slide MHS 02 7451 3 contains a tissue fragment showing low grade invasive ductal carcinoma and ductal carcinoma in situ  This fragment is not present on the duplicate tissue profile on this slide  nor is it present on any of the other 3 slides  In addition the duplicate tissue profile on this slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  shows a separate tissue fragment with apparent invasive carcinoma  This tissue fragment is not present on the first profile of this slide or on any of the other 3 slides  Given that each of the fragments with carcinoma are present on opposite tissue profiles of one slide and are not on any of the other slides  and given that most of the tissue fragments in this specimen consist only of a adipose tissue  the possibility that the fragments with carcinoma are derived from another case needs to be given serious consideration  CLINICAL DATA  History  Breast biopsy  TISSUE SUBMITTED  Consult slides  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by WITKIEWICZ AGNIESKA K  M D  Received from Life Laboratories Mercy Hospital  144 State Street  Springfield  MA REMOVED_CASE_ID  are thirty five  35  slides  Four  4  slides are labeled  MHS 02 REMOVED_CASE_ID  and sublabeled  H E    2    3   and  recut   corresponding to a right breast core biopsy  obtained on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying report bearing the patient s name  Thirty one  31  slides are labeled  MHS 02 REMOVED_CASE_ID  and sublabeled  1A  through  23A  and  1B  through  8B   corresponding to two right breast excisions  5 x 4 5 x 4 cm and 4 x 3 x 1 cm   obtained REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying report bearing the patient s name  Reports to  MATORY  YVEDT  L  M D  SPECIMEN TYPE  OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT   BREAST ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE  OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT   BREAST  report_end , 0.
