Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY   PARTIAL OR SIMPLE Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  LESTER  SUSAN  M D  PH D  DIAGNOSIS  by LESTER SUSAN M D  PH D  RIGHT BREAST  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  Benign mass forming lesion of the breast  11 cm  consisting predominantly of hypocellular interlobular stroma with sparse small hyalinized lobular units  see NOTE   Peripheral tissue with normocellular breast parenchyma and normal stroma  Cysts with apocrine metaplasia  Epithelial hyperplasia  Biopsy site with repair reaction  NOTE  Almost the entire breast is replaced by a circumscribed area of very dense breast tissue with almost no intervening adipose tissue  This lesion could be classified as a  fibrous tumor  of the breast which is a benign  self limited proliferation  Reference  PP Rosen  Rosen s Brast Pathology  pages REMOVED_DATE  CLINICAL DATA  History  A 28 year old premenopausal female with a globally tender and enlarging right breast  mammogram on REMOVED_DATE  and ultrasound on REMOVED_DATE  were unrevealing  while an MRI revealed scant fat and no defined mass  and a REMOVED_DATE  right breast biopsy revealed dense hyalinized breast parenchyma with no carcinoma seen  breast continues to enlarge  patients grandmother was treated for a phyllodes tumor   Operation  Right Skin Sparing Mastectomy with Lateral flap implant Clinical Diagnosis  Right breast carcinoma TISSUE SUBMITTED   1  Right breast  long suture lateral   short suture superior  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by GREISMAN HARVEY A  M D  PH D  The specimen is received fresh  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  date of birth and   1  right breast   and consists of a 185 gm skin sparing mastectomy specimen  12 3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  with a white tan skin ellipse  4 2 x 3 7 cm  containing the nipple  The skin is oriented with a short stitch superior and a long stitch lateral  There is a REMOVED_DATE cm semicircular scar in the upper outer quadrant of the nipple and an underlying biopsy site  3 x 3 cm   There is a white tan fibrous mass  11 cm  replacing the entire lateral aspect of the breast  approximately 85  of the total tissue  and extending to the posterior margin  which is inked in black  There is a small amount  15   of tan yellow fibroadipose tissue at the medial aspect of the specimen that is grossly consistent with normal breast tissue  Photographs are taken and tissue is sent for cytogenetics  Micro 1  mass and posterior margin  lateral  1 fragment  RSS  Micro 2  mass and posterior margin  upper outer quadrant  1 fragment  RSS  Micro 3  mass and posterior margin  upper inner quadrant  1 fragment  RSS  Micro 4  mass and posterior margin  lower inner quadrant  2 fragments  RSS  Micro 5  mass and posterior margin  inferior  1 fragment  RSS  Micro 6  mass and posterior margin  lower outer quadrant  1 fragment  RSS  Micro 7  mass and medial fibroadipose tissue  1 fragment  RSS  Micro REMOVED_DATE  medial fibroadipose tissue  2 fragments  RSS  Micro 10  biopsy site  2 fragments  RSS  Micro 11  biopsy site and skin  2 fragments  RSS  Micro REMOVED_DATE  nipple  perpendicular  2 fragments  RSS  Reports to  KAELIN  CAROLYN  MARY M D  SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST MASTECTOMY   PARTIAL OR SIMPLE  report_end , 0.
