e medial  posterior  and inferior margins  The mass is present REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin  REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin  and more than 3 cm from the superior margin  There is a cavity  1 1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  containing amorphous debris present more superiorly within the excision specimen  grossly 0 5 cm from the posterior margin  REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin  and greater than 2 cm from the remaining margins  This cavity is grossly consistent with an abscess cavity and is surrounded by tan  discolored fat with focal chalky areas  consistent with fat necrosis  Representative sections are submitted for microscopic examination  Micro REMOVED_DATE  well circumscribed mass  2 frag  RSS Micro REMOVED_DATE  abscess cavity  6 frag  RSS Micro REMOVED_DATE  additional sections of encapsulated mass  3 frag  RSS Micro REMOVED_DATE  cystic abscess  3 frag  RSS Part two   right breast tissue at 8 o clock short superior  long lateral   consists of a yellow to focally pink breast excision specimen  2 9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE  cm  which includes two  2  sutures placed by the surgeon to designate the superior and lateral orientation  The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins  posterior   black  anterior   blue  superior   red  inferior   green  lateral   yellow  medial   orange  Sectioning from inferior to superior reveals a poorly circumscribed  firm  gold to tan mass  1 8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  with a central cavity filled with amorphous debris  The mass grossly abuts all margins  The specimen is entirely submitted for microscopic examination  Micro REMOVED_DATE  breast mass  8 o clock  8 frag  ESS rlr Reports to  CARTER  KATHARINE M D  SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST BIOPSY W O MARGINS ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST BIOPSY W O MARGINS  report_end , 0.
