Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Specimen Type  Consult slides Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  MEHRA GOLSHAN M D  CASE  BS 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PATIENT  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME Resident  Mingjian J You  M D   Ph D  Pathologist  Susan Lester  M D   Ph D  PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS  CONSULT SLIDES FROM FAULKNER HOSPITAL  BOSTON  MA  RIGHT BREAST  UPPER INNER  1 00  ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A 0 7 CM NODULE  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_DATE    INVASIVE CARCINOMA MOST CONSISTENT WITH ADENOID CYSTIC CARCINOMA  grade 1  measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size  see note   No lymphovascular invasion is present  Immunoperoxidase studies were performed with the following results for invasive carcinoma  reviewed   Estrogen receptor NEGATIVE Progesterone receptor NEGATIVE REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu NEGATIVE  0  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID POSITIVE in most tumor cells Cytokeratin PANK POSITIVE in most tumor cells Cytokeratin HMW POSITIVE in most tumor cells Actin POSITIVE in most tumor cells Epithelial membrane antigen POSITIVE in a minority of tumor Cells Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen and progesterone receptors  Note  The carcinoma has two cell populations consistent with both luminal and myoepithelial differentiation  In this biopsy  the findings would be consistent with adenoid cystic carcinoma  Final classification should be determined after complete excision  It is difficult to distinguish invasion from DCIS in carcinomas of this type  due to the positivity for myoepithelial markers in the tumor cells  There may be an adjacent component of DCIS  CLINICAL DATA  History  Dense and nodular right breast  pain upper inner  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm nodule Clinical Diagnosis  IDC TISSUE SUBMITTED  Consult slides  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received from Faulkner Hospital  Pathology Department  1153 Centre Street  Boston  MA REMOVED_CASE_ID  are ten  10  glass slides  T