Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  01 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 37 CLINICAL DATA  Patient has a suspicious exam and a mammagram that is also suspicious for malignancy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  100    EXTENDS TO THE BIOPSY MARGIN  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 04                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab labeled with the patient s name  unit number and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragments of tissue  After inking  sectioning reveal tan red fleshy ill defined area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  In addition there is an adjacent well defined light tan nodule  A representative section of the ill defined mass is submitted as FX 1 and the block is kept frozen  A smaller fragment on cut section reveals tan firm tissue with a white rim  Cassette A contain the  adjacent nodule   B through D contain the mass and cassette E contains a smaller nodule  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST MASS   INVASIVE ADENOCARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Jay Austen  MD O R  Diagnosis by  James F  Southern  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS  report_end , 0.
