Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 20 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   RE EXCISION  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 1 OF 12 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Residual carcinoma is not identified in the re excision specimen  The metastatic focus spans REMOVED_DATE cm  and it does not transgress the lymph node capsule  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 41                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary contents  is a portion of fibrofatty tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  Within the soft tissue is a fluid filled cyst measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm filled with clear yellow fluid  There are fifteen tan rubbery nodules ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  Section Code  A  representative wall of the cyst  B  halves of two bisected lymph nodes  C E  remaining lymph nodes  Received fresh  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a portion of oriented breast measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  There is a overlying skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with a central area of ulceration measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  There is a long suture designating the lateral breast and a short suture designating the superior breast  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal the primary pathology to be located in the inferior portion of the breast  There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm area of bright yellow firm breast tissue located subjacent to the deep medial margin  The biopsy cavity extends to REMOVED_DATE cm beneath the skin margin detected by areas of fibrous tissue  Section Code  F  area of bright yellow firm breast parenchyma located in the inferior breast  G H  entire cross section of inferior breast including biopsy cavity and overlying biopsy site  I  midway between the inferior and superior portion of breast tissue  This is the biopsy cavity of the lateral tissue with overlying skin  J  representative section of normal breast with overlying skin and ulcer  Resident  ERIN OCHOA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST  RE EXCISION PART B  LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  report_end , 1.
