or  In addition  there is a needle which has been placed by radiology  though the needle was no longer in place when it was received in pathology  The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal fibrofatty breast tissue with no discrete masses or nodules  There are occasional fibrous foci  There was no blue inked present on the specimen  anterior margin   Representative sections are submitted as follows  Micro 1  Superior  medial  and skin margins  1 frag  RSS  Micro 2  Inferior and medial margins  1 frag  RSS  Micro 3  Superior with skin  1 frag  RSS  Micro 4  Posterior and inferior  1 frag  RSS  Micro 5  Inferior  1 frag  RSS  Micro 6  Posterior  inferior  superior  2 frags  RSS  Micro 7  Lateral  superior  inferior  1 frag  RSS  Micro 8  Inferior and superior  1 frag  RSS  Micro 9  Posterior  superior  inferior  1 frag  RSS  Micro 10  Inferior  superior  1 frag  RSS  Micro 11  Inferior  superior  2 frags  RSS  Micro 12  Lateral  2 frags  RSS  Part two  labeled   2  Superior shave margin   consists of fibrofatty breast tissue  5 6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm   designated by the surgeon with a short stitch superior and the superior portion is inked red  The remainder of the specimen is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal mostly soft yellow adipost tissue with some areas of white fibrous tissue which extends to the red inked margin  All fragments containing fibrous tissue are submitted  Representative sections are submitted as follows  Micro REMOVED_DATE  Shave margin  multi frags  RSS  pes Reports to  CHRISTIAN  ROGER  L  M D  SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE  SURGICAL MARGIN  report_end , 1.
