 mammo   short superior  long lateral  RADIOGRAPHY REPORT  Central lesion and three  3  wires in specimen  A Elmar  GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph labeled with the patient s name and date of birth  showing the x ray of the specimen with three localization wires and three densities  with the main one circled by the radiologist  The specimen is received fresh in one part  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and   1   left breast tissue at 12 o clock  short superior  long lateral    and consists of one fragment of fibroadipose breast tissue  9 0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm   Three wires enter the specimen at the medial anterior aspect  Two orienting sutures are designated by the surgeon  with a short suture indicating the superior aspect and a long suture indicating the lateral aspect of the specimen  The specimen is inked according to the pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins  posterior black  anterior blue  superior red  inferior green  lateral yellow  medial orange  It is sectioned medial to lateral to reveal four different potential lesions  The first  most lateral lesion  mass  1   is a hard white gray nodule located in slice two  associated with calcifications  0 5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  located REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin  In the same slice  slice two  there is another area of hard  ill defined breast tissue  mass  2   with several calcifications  2 5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  located REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin  The distance between the first and second mass in slice two is REMOVED_DATE cm  Both the second and first masses abut the anterior margin  with the first one being more superior to the second one  Slice three has some hemorrhage in the breast tissue  Slice four contains the main mass  mass  3  which is hard and ill defined  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  and located REMOVED_DATE cm