Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 30 CLINICAL DATA  52 year old with mammogram revealing large calcified spiculated mass  Superior and lateral right breast  Core biopsy of this today  Abnormal calcification lower inner quadrant of the right breast  localized right breast biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   WITH INCISIONAL BIOPSY OF PALPABLE LESION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The entire REMOVED_DATE cm incisional biopsy consists of carcinoma  There is no evidence of an in situ component or vascular space invasion  Receptor studies are pending and will be reported in an addendum  BREAST  RIGHT  NEEDLE LOCALIZED   BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH FIBROSIS  CYSTS  SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  ATYPICAL DUCTAL EPITHELIAL HYPERPLASIA  AND MICROCALCIFICATIONS  Diagnosis by  Teri L  Cooper Moore MD Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 21                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT  NEEDLE LOCALIZATION   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 28 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of irregular pink tan rubbery tissue and fat  Frozen entirely as frozen section  1  and resubmitted as J  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a localizing wire and accompanying specimen x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal no grossly suspicious foci  The specimen is submitted entirely in A through I  with microcalcified area in B through E  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST  CORE BIOPSY  POORLY  DIFFERENTIATED INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Benjamin Alan Spencer  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST CORE BIOPSY PART B  NEEDLE LOCALIZED BIOPSY  report_end , 0.
