Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID LUMPECTOMY Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  FARVER  CAROL  FRANCIS  MD DIAGNOSIS  by FARVER CAROL FRANCIS MD LEFT BREAST LUMPECTOMY  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE cm  moderately differentiated  modified Bloom Richardson II III  see note   Tumor is present at one inked surgical margin  block  5   ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  one focus  AXILLARY CONTENTS  Thirteen  13  lymph nodes with no tumor seen  NOTE  The tumor has focal ductal features  but is histologically similar to the previous biopsy  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   CLINICAL DATA  History  None given  TISSUE SUBMITTED   1  Left breast mass   2  Axillary contents  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by DUTTA ANINDYA M B  B S  PH D  The specimen is received fresh in two parts  The first part  labelled  left breast mass  is a 5 x 5 x 3 cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a central cavity measuring 3 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm  The cavity is almost completely closed except for a central opening measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and the wall of the cavity is thinnest at a thickness of REMOVED_DATE cm  The interior of the cavity wall was inked along side the external surface  A hard white tissue constitutes most of the cavity wall and extends to the inked outer surface  Micro  1  Section through the cavity wall  including both the interior surface of the cavity and exterior surface  Micro  2  Sections similar to the one above but from the opposite surface  Micros  3 7  Sections through the outer wall of the mass  so that the only inked margin is the outer wall of the mass from each of the surfaces that had not been sectioned in micros number one and two  Hard white tissue constitute most of the wall of the cavity and extends up to the outer most inked surface  The second part  labelled  axillary nodes  is 8 x 8 x 6 cm piece of fibrofatty tissue bearing lymph nodes  Eleven lymph nodes were found  the largest measuring 2 cm in length  Micros  8 10  Eleven frags  lymph nodes  RSS  Reports to  OSTEEN  ROBERT  T  M D  SPECIMEN TYPE  LUMPECTOMY  report_end , 1.
