Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT   BREAST Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  LESTER  SUSAN  M D  PH D  DIAGNOSIS  by LESTER SUSAN M D  PH D  CONSULT SLIDES AND PARAFFIN BLOCKS FROM ST  MARY S REGIONAL MEDICAL CENTER  LEWISTON  ME  RIGHT BREAST  CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES OF A MASS  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_DATE    HIGH GRADE MALIGNANT UNDIFFERENTIATED SMALL BLUE CELL NEOPLASM  see Comment below   RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE EXCISION AND INCISIONAL BREAST BIOPSY  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  5 19 04   RIGHT BREAST  INCISIONAL BIOPSY  HIGH GRADE MALIGNANT SMALL BLUE CELL NEOPLASM WITH NEURAL DIFFERENTIATION  see Comment below   A minute area of bone formation is present within the tumor  The tumor infiltrates in normal breast parenchyma  Note  This was a small biopsy measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE  METASTATIC HIGH GRADE MALIGNANT SMALL BLUE CELL NEOPLASM WITH NEURAL DIFFERENTIATION  is present within a lymph node  The node measured 5 cm and appears to be almost completely replaced by the tumor  The tumor has two components  One component consists of small blue cells  round or with tapering ends  with hyperchromatic nuclei and a high mitotic rate  These cells have an undifferentiated or  blastema  appearance  This cell population merges into the second component that consists predominantly of neuropil with occasional larger cells with the appearance of ganglion cells  consistent with neural differentiaion  Immunoperoxidase studies were performed at BWH and at the original institution with the following results  Small blue cells Differentiated REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID FOCAL  WEAK FOCAL Synaptophysin POSITIVE  WEAK POSITIVE Neuron specific enolase FOCAL POSITIVE  STRONG Chromogranin NEGATIVE NEGATIVE Glial fibrillary acidic protein NEGATIVE POSITIVE  STRONG REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  NEGATIVE NEGATIVE Neurofilament protein NEGATIVE NEGATIVE Cytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID POSITIVE  FOCAL NEGATIVE Cytokeratin PANK POSITIVE NEGATIVE Cytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 2 POSITIVE NEGATIVE Vimentin POSITIVE POSITIVE Alpha feto protein NEGATIVE NEGATIVE HEP PAR NEGATIVE NEGATIVE Carcinoembryonic antigen   p NEGATIVE NEGATIVE Desmin NEGATIVE NEGATIVE Myf 4 NEGATIVE NEGATIVE Note  The small blue cells do not have the immunophenotype specific for either neuroblastoma or hepatoblastoma  The immunoperoxidase studies support neural differentiation in the second component of the tumor  The overall impression is that of a neoplasm consisting of undifferentiated cells with the capacity to differentiate into neural tissue  The only other possible differentiated component is a minute area of bone  This case was also reviewed by Dr  Christopher Fletcher and Dr  Antonio Nascimento  Mayo Clinic  and both favored a high grade malignant neuroblastic neoplasm  consistent with differentiating neuroblastoma  This is a highly unusual neoplasm that has not been described previously in the breast or at other sites  The possibility of metastasis from another site has been considered clinically  However  the only identified sites of disease are the breast  axillary lymph nodes  and internal mammary nodes  CLINICAL DATA  History  The patient is a 34 year old woman who gave birth to her third child in REMOVED_MONTH 2003  In REMOVED_MONTH while breast feeding  she developed breast fullness and hardness which became painful  She underwent FNA and then core needle biopsy  A CT scan showed the large mass completely replacing the breast and an 8 to 9 cm hemangioma of the right lobe of the liver  but no other masses or lymphadenopathy  PET showed the large breast mass and internal mammary lymph nodes  but no other sites of involvement  The liver mass was not positive  consistent with a hemangioma  She subsequently underwent excision of a palpable axillary lymph node and an incisional biopsy of the breast  Clinical Diagnosis  High grade neuroblastic neoplasm  TISSUE SUBMITTED  Consult slides and paraffin blocks  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by LOMO LESLEY C  M D  Received from St  Mary s Regional Medical Center  Pathology Department  Campus Avenue  P O  Box 291  Lewiston  ME REMOVED_DATE  are fifteen  15  slides and six paraffin blocks  Two  2  slides are labeled  S 04 2341  and sublabeled  1  1   and  2  3    corresponding to a right breast core needle biopsy performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient s name  Thirteen  13  slides and six  6  paraffin blocks are labeled  S 04 2534   the slides are sublabeled  1 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  2     2 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  2   and  1 A  2     1 B  2     1B KERATIN    1B MIC 2    1B SYNAPTO    1B VIM    1B GFAP    1 C  2  through  1 F  2    and the paraffin blocks are sublabeled  1A  through  1F   corresponding to a right axillary lymph node excision  5 x 4 x 2 cm  and right breast incisional biopsy performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient s name  Included is a consultation report from Mayo Clinic  Rochester  MN  numbered  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and dated REMOVED_DATE  corresponding to the case listed above  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  bearing the patient s name  By report  molecular studies for synovial sarcoma associated gene rearrangements were negative  Also included is a consultation report from Mayo Clinic  Rochester  MN  numbered  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and dated REMOVED_DATE  referrring institution St  Mary s Regional Medical Center  Lewiston  ME  their accession number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  bearing the patient s name  Included also are two  2  consultation letters  one  1  letter dated REMOVED_DATE  from Dr  Daniel W  Visscher at Mayo Clinic  Rochester  MN  to Dr  Alan R  Solander at St  Mary s Regional Medical Center  referring to the case listed above  S 04 2341   the second letter is dated REMOVED_DATE  from Dr  Antonio G  Nascimento at Mayo Clinic Rochester  MN  to Dr  Richard Malone at St  Mary s Regional Hospital  Lewinston  ME  referring to the case listed above  S 04 2534   bearing the patient s name  Also included is an oncology consultation report from The Regional Center for Cancer and Blood Disorders  affiliated with St  Mary s Regional Medical Center  dated REMOVED_DATE  and signed by Dr  Amir H  Modarressi  bearing the patient s name  Reports to  GOLSHAN  MEHRA M D  SPECIMEN TYPE  OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT   BREAST ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE  OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT   BREAST  report_end , 0.
