ion wire and the second set of radiographs have no localization wire  Part A    1  Right needle localized breast mass   consists of an unoriented skin ellipse  3 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm   The deepest aspect of the specimen is comprised of the deep firm white tissue  approximately REMOVED_DATE x 3 8 x REMOVED_DATE cm  Overall dimension of the specimen excluding the localization wire is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  The surgical margins are inked blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a homogeneous but variegated yellow to white firm mass at the dimension previously described  The remainder of the specimen is lobulated yellow adipose tissue  The region of the wire tip is found in cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the specimen is sectioned and submitted in its entirety  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Firm white region of specimen  localization wire region in cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  multi frags  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Superior portion of specimen with skin ellipse  multi frags  ESS  Part B    2  Re excision RT breast mass REMOVED_DATE    consists of an unoriented fragment of fibroadipose soft tissue  4 8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm   with no localization wire  The mass is almost entirely comprised of firm  white fibrous tissue  with only a thin border of adipose tissue on one edge  The outer surface of the entire specimen is inked blue  Sectioning reveals a solid white mass with a small yellow punctate region  and focal areas of hemorrhage and fibrosis  The specimen is submitted in its entirety  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  White mass with attached adipose tissue  multi frags  ESS  Note  Part B container came with two labels  both designated   2  Re excision RT breast mass REMOVED_DATE    and due to the submission of two form 86 for the same number  specimen labels have been attached to the back of the form 86  CASE NUMBER  BG 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID By his her signature below  the senior physician