Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 03 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 12 08 CLINICAL DATA  37 year old female patient with one month history of increasing shortness of breath  chest pain  Large anterior mediastinal mass  increasing nodes  left breast mass  pericardial and pleural effusions with cardiac tamponade    lymphoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT MASS   BIOPSY  BENIGN BREAST TISSUE WITH NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  MEDIASTINUM  MASS   BIOPSY  MEDIASTINAL  THYMIC  LARGE B CELL LYMPHOMA  SEE NOTE   NOTE  The tumor comprises sheets of large lymphoid cells with irregular  vesicular nuclei  distinct nucleoli  and abundant pale to clear cytoplasm  These cells are admixed with varying numbers of histiocytes  small lymphocytes  and neutrophils in a background of loose fibrosis  Diagnosis by  ROBERT P  HASSERJIAN  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 13 01                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS ON PARAFFIN SECTIONS  With antibody to B lineage antigen REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID there is staining of most large cells in a diffuse pattern  The B cells are negative for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  With antibody to T lineage associated antigen REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID there is staining of some small cells scattered within the tissue  With antibody to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID many large cells are stained in a perinuclear dot pattern  but show no membrane staining  The large tumor cells are also positive for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and are weakly focally positive for REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa  Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results confirm the diagnosis of B cell lymphoma  See note  NOTE  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  ROBERT P  HASSERJIAN  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 16 16     FLOW CYTOMETRY Addendum     FLOW CYTOMETRY REPORT  Hematopoietic Cell Surface Markers SPECIMEN  Tissue  Mediastinal Mass REMOVED_DATE cm RECEIVED  REMOVED_DATE  DIFFERENTIAL COUNT  light scatter   Lymphocytes  77  Monocytes  6  Granulocytes  13  Debris    RESULTS                  LIGHT SCATTER GATE ANALYZED  Lymphocyte ANTIGENS  T CELL B CELL MYELOID OTHER                                                               REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  28  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  69  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  90  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 4  21  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  69  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  6  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 8  7  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID KAPPA   1  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 45     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  29  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID LAMBDA   1  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  32  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 20 5  1  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 20 10  21 dim REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 20 23  2  HLA DR    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 20 43  52  TdT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    MPO    INTERPRETATION  1  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDdim  cells without surface immunoglobulin light chain expression  2  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  T cells  see note   Note  This immunophenotype in combination with the morphologic features is consistent with a diagnosis of B cell lymphoma   Analysis by Frederic I  Preffer  PhD  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  ROBERT P  HASSERJIAN  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 16 20     CYTOGENETICS Addendum     ACCESSION NUMBER  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID DATE RECEIVED  REMOVED_DATE  REPORT DATE  REMOVED_DATE  CELL ORIGIN  Lymph Node KARYOTYPE  46 XX t 9 21  p22 q22  10  46 XX 4  METAPHASES COUNTED  14 ANALYZED  4 SCORED  0 BANDING  GTG INTERPRETATION  Ten of 14 metaphase cells contained a clonal translocation t 9 21   which is not known to be characteristic of any particular type of tumor  COMMENTS  INDICATION FOR TEST  Assessment for lymphoma CLINICAL DATA  37 year old female This test was performed at the Cytogenetics Laboratory located at Brigham and Women s Hospital  75 Francis Street  Boston  MA REMOVED_CASE_ID  Added by  SHENG XIAO  MD Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 09 24 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled with the patient s name and unit number and  left breast mass  are multiple yellow soft tissue fragments measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate  The specimen is entirely frozen as FX 1  now resubmitted in cassette A  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled with the patient s name and unit number  and  mediastinal mass  are multiple tan grey rubbery soft tissue fragments measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate  Representative sections are frozen as FX 2  and saved frozen  Representative sections of the non frozen tissue fragments are fixed in B plus  now resubmitted in cassette B  and formalin  now resubmitted in cassettes C D   Representative samples for cytogenetics and flow cytometry are sent  Resident  ANDRAS SCHAFFER  MD PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 LEFT BREAST MASS BIOPSY  BREAST TISSUE WITH FIBROSIS  THER