Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SKIN  OTHER THAN CYST  TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  MCKEE  PHILLIP  H   M D  DIAGNOSIS  by MCKEE PHILLIP H  M D  1  SKIN  UPPER MEDIAL LEFT BREAST  The sections show skin with minimal subcutaneous fat  A large particle of calcified material is present in the lower reticular dermis  This does not represent calciphylaxis  There is no evidence of vasculitis or thrombosis  Multiple levels examined  2  SKIN  MEDIAL LATERAL LEFT BREAST  The sections show skin and subcutaneous fat  Necrotic epidermis with underlying regenerating epithelium is noted  There is no evidence of vasculitis  thrombosis or calciphylaxis  3  CORE BIOPSY  LEFT BREAST  The sections show multiple fragments of breast parenchyma plus fibrofatty tissue  The latter shows focal necrosis  widespread infarction and thrombosed vessels  A fibrin stain is positive  No evidence of calciphylaxis is seen and a von Kossa stain is negative  The features are certainly consistent with a hypercoagulable state  They could be related to the prior episode of Coumadin therapy  There is no evidence of a vasculitis  Multiple levels examined  CLINICAL DATA  History  Calciphylaxis  parathryoidectomy  failed renal transplant 1988 and 2000  Operation  Excisions  Clinical Diagnosis  ESRD  TISSUE SUBMITTED  Skin  1  Upper medial left breast  2  Medial lateral left breast  3  Core biopsy  left breast  multiple  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by KWAAN MARY R  M D  The specimen is received fresh  in three parts  each labeled with the patient s name and unit number  Part 1   Upper medial lt breast skin   consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan  unoriented elliptical skin  There is a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm red tan  ill defined  hyperemic lesion which extends to multiple radial margins  The specimen is inked  sectioned and entirely submitted  Micro 1  Skin  end   2 fra