Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W O MARGINS Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  NASH  SHIRIN  VIMADALAL  M D  DIAGNOSIS  by NASH SHIRIN VIMADALAL M D  1  RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY  Fibrocystic change  focally proliferative with dense stromal fibrosis  Extensive perivascular lymphocytic infiltration composed of small lymphoid cells  including round and occasional notched or irregular forms  Note  The extent of the infiltrate raises the possibility of involvement by a lymphoproliferative disorder  However  a definitive diagnosis cannot be based solely on this material  Special studies will be performed in an attempt to phenotype these cells  If a peripheral lymphocytosis is present  assessment of immunoglobulin light chains  for possible B cell clonal excess  may be helpful in further evaluation  SURGICAL ADDENDUM  by NASH SHIRIN VIMADALAL M D  Immunoperoxidase studies show that the lymphoid cells are predominantly B cells Scanty lymphoid cells also stain with anti Leu 22 and anti UCHL 1  These studies are not diagnostic  Although a diagnosis of a lymphoproliferative disorder cannot be made  it cannot be ruled out See note above CLINICAL DATA  History  None given  TISSUE SUBMITTED  Right breast biopsy  O R  CONSULTATION  RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY  Fibrofatty breast tissue  no areas grossly suspicious for malignancy  RIGHT BREAST TISSUE FOR FROZEN  FSA   Fibrous breast tissue  No evidence of malignancy  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by FLAX JONATHAN DAVID M D  The specimen  received in fixative  in two containers  The first specimen  labelled  right breast biopsy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of white  rubbery tissue  Micros  1 5  Right breast biopsy  ESS  8 frags  1 cass  The second specimen  labelled  right breast  frozen   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm firm  white  soft tissue fragment  The firmest portion of which was frozen  FS A   Micro