Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 06 CLINICAL DATA  Mammographic abnormality of right breast  New findings   on physical exam  some thickening at 10 o clock  2 cm lateral to areola  No palpable breast masses  supraclavicular or axillary lymph nodes  No family history of breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING  70   INTRADUCTAL  30   CARCINOMA   0 8 CM   GRADE I II III  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Tumor extends to within less than REMOVED_DATE cm of inked resection margin  The tumor is focally cytologically well differentiated with uniform cells filling ducts without necrosis  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 41                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 09 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab  labeled with the patient s name  unit number and  right breast tissue  is a 4 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm piece of yellow fatty tissue with a firm area palpated and a localizing needle in place with an accompanying x ray  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal fibrofatty breast tissue with a firm stellate lesion  measuring REMOVED_DATE cm greatest dimension  Representative section frozen as FX  1 and saved frozen  The remainder submitted is A F  Resident  James Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST RIGHT   INFILTRATING AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Douglas B  Flieder  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST TISSUE  report_end , 0.
