Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W O MARGINS Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  MUTTER  GEORGE  LUTHER  M D  DIAGNOSIS  by MUTTER GEORGE LUTHER M D  SPECIMEN LABELED  RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY   Atypical ductal hyperplasia  extensive  micropapillary type  See comment  Fibrocystic changes  proliferative  COMMENT  Criteria for a diagnosis of carcinoma in situ are not met in any of the slides examined  although the degree of atypia is extreme  SPECIMEN LABELED  ENDOCERVICAL CURETTINGS   Negative endocervix with squamous metaplasia  SPECIMEN LABELED  ENDOMETRIAL CURETTINGS   Proliferative endometrium  Negative endocervix  Lower uterine segment  SURGICAL ADDENDUM  by MUTTER GEORGE LUTHER M D  The right breast biopsy was reveiwed at the request of Dr  Christine Denison  and the following addendum prepared in consultation with Dr  Susan Lester  As stated in the original report  there is an extensive micropapillary lesion with severe atypia  Focal areas of epithelial cell necrosis and calcification are present within the lesion and likely correspond to the fine calcifications present mammographically  This is an unsual lesion and difficult to classify  Some observors favor a diagnosis of ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA WITH SEVERE ATYPIA  i e  bordening on carcinoma in situ  for the entire lesion whereas others would classify some areas as DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Clinical correlation is advised  CLINICAL DATA  History  Calcification right breast  bleeding polymenorrhea  Operation  Right breast biopsy needle directed  D C  Operative findings  Calification right breast Clinical Diagnosis  Calficiation right breast  polymenorrhea  TISSUE SUBMITTED   1  Right breast mass  2  Endocervical curettings  3  Endometrial curettings O R  CONSULTATION  SPECIMEN LABELED  RIGHT BREAST MASS   No gross evidence of infiltrating malignancy  Await permanents  RADIOLOGY  The Ca  are in the specimen  E  Wa