Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W O MARGINS Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  MARTIN REAY  DAVID  MD DIAGNOSIS  by MARTIN REAY DAVID MD BREAST  RIGHT EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  2 2 cm   poorly differentiated   Modified Bloom Richardson Grade III III   see note   Infiltrating tumor is present at multiple surgical resection margins  The in situ component has high grade nuclear features  is within the tumor and accounts for less than 5  of the entire tumor mass  Lymphatic invasion present  NOTE  There is a marked lymphocytic response to the tumor and multiple protrusions of tumor from the main mass which accounts for the decrepancy in measurement at the time of O R  consultation  Tissue was submitted for ER PR and flow cytometric analysis  CLINICAL DATA  History  Lesion sutured to show its in situ orientation  Operation  Excision mass right breast  Clinical Diagnosis  Right breast mass  TISSUE SUBMITTED  Breast tissue  O R  CONSULTATION  SPECIMEN LABELED  RIGHT BREAST MASS   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE cm  Tissue sent for ER PR and flow  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by KRANE JEFFREY FRED M D  PH D  Received fresh  labeled with the patient s name  unit number and  right breast mass   is a 5 x 3 x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue with a firm tan white irregular gritty area REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter  A portion of the gritty area is submitted as frozen section A  Tissue is also submitted for ER PR and flow cytometric analysis  MICRO  1  FSRA  1 frag  ESS  MICRO  2  Tissue adjacent to frozen section  1 frag  ESS  MICRO  3 10  Remainder of fibrous breast tissue  90  of total tissue  100  of fibrous tissue  9 frags  RSS  Reports to  SPIEVACK  ALAN  R  M D  SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST BIOPSY W O MARGINS  report_end , 0.
Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 06 CLINICAL DATA  Rule out breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  100    MODERATE TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE INKED RESECTION MARGINS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures approximately REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension by gross examination  No definite vascular invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 35                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 07 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled with the patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of pink tan fibrofatty breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal pink and white  shiny  semifirm cut surface  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  The remaining tissue is submitted entirely in A through B  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST LEFT BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  EXTENDING TO THE MARGINS  O R  Resident  SCOTT D  URBAN  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS  report_end , 0.
