Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT   BREAST Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  RICHARDSON  ANDREA  L   M D  PH D  DIAGNOSIS  by RICHARDSON ANDREA L  M D  PH D  CONSULT SLIDES FROM BROCKTON HOSPITAL  BROCKTON  MA  RIGHT BREAST  AXILLA  EXCISION OF A MASS  04 3165 4 8 04   UNUSUAL FIBROEPITHELIAL NEOPLASM  with features intermediate between a papilloma and a cellular fibroadenoma  The epithelial component is columnar hyperplasia with flat atypia and single cell necrosis  No areas of classic atypical ductal hyperplasia or diagnostic ductal carcinoma in situ are seen  The stromal component is moderately cellular with no atypia  stromal overgrowth  or mitotic activity  The margins of the lesion are predominantly circumscribed  but areas of stromal infiltration into surrounding fat are noted  There is a prominent area of lesion necrosis  possibly related to infarction or to a prior needle procedure  Clinical correlation is required  The lesions extends to inked margins  Given the unusual features  complete excision is recommended  CLINICAL DATA  History  None given  TISSUE SUBMITTED  Consult slides  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by KUTEN ADAM M D  Received from Brockton Hospital  Pathology Department  680 Brockton Street  Brockton  MA REMOVED_CASE_ID  are two  2  slides  The slides are labeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and sublabeled  A  and  B   corresponding to a right breast  axilla mass performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient s name  Included is a consultation report from New York Presbyterian Hospital  New York  NY  numbered  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and dated REMOVED_DATE  referring to the case listed above bearing the patient s name  Reports to  GOLSHAN  MEHRA M D  SPECIMEN TYPE  OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT   BREAST  report_end , 1.
