 1850 gram modified radical mastectomy specimen  measuring 22 cm medially to laterally  REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior  and REMOVED_DATE cm deep  There is an overlying ellipse of pale skin  REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral  and REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior  Located REMOVED_DATE cm lateral to the medial pole of this skin ellipse is a REMOVED_DATE cm diameter unremarkable areola within which there is a REMOVED_DATE  cm diameter grossly normal nipple  REMOVED_DATE cm superior to the superior aspect of the areola there is a 5 cm long fresh incision  The deep margin of the specimen is defined by a smooth fascial plane and along the lateral aspect of the specimen there is a 6 x REMOVED_DATE cm x REMOVED_DATE cm axillary tail  Located REMOVED_DATE cm deep to the incision there is a 3 x 3 x 2 cm fresh biopsy cavity that comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep margin  Just inferior to the biopsy site  deep to the areola  is an ill defined 2 x 2 x 2 cm area of white fibrous tissue with foci of creamy yellow necrotic material grossly suspicious for comedo carcinoma  The presence of infiltrating tumor cannot be ruled out by gross exam  Superior and lateral to the biopsy cavity there are several strands of white fibrous tissue within which are ropey and nodular densities grossly suspicious for comedo carcinoma  However  gross evidence of invasive tumor is not present within this area  MICRO  10 15  Sections adjacent to biopsy cavity  including deep margin  RSS  mult frags  6 cass  MICRO  16 and 17  Sections from dense area inferior to biopsy cavity  RSS  2 frags  2 cass  MICRO  18 and 19  Sections from ropey area  inferior and lateral to inferior and lateral to biopsy site  RSS  2 frags  2 cass  MICRO  20  Upper inner quadrant  RSS  1 frag  1 cass  MICRO  21  Lower inner quadrant  RSS  1 frag  1 cass  MICRO  22  Upper outer quadrant  RSS  1 frag  1 cass  MICRO  23  Lower outer quadrant  RSS  1 frag  1 cass  MICRO  24  Nipple and skin incision site  RSS  1