pletely leveled through  The pools of mucin are worrisome for mucinous carcinoma  however  a diagnosis of mucinous carcinoma cannot be made on this material given the lack of atypical epithelial cells within the mucin  Radiographic pathologic correlation is recommended and repeat biopsies may be indicated  especially if a mass lesion is identified  Final Diagnosis by  Nicole A  Mihok  M D  DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT   Continued  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    1223 PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    1308 MD MIHN Notes  REMOVED_DATE  In addition to the cosigner Dr  Abbott  Dr  Mattia has reviewed the case and concurs with the diagnosis  NAM Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    1224 PAT MURJCODES  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Epithelium  NOS REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Right breast  N Needle REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Right breast  N Mucin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Adipose tissue BREANBX    BREANBX BREANBX REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    BREANBX Separation  NOS Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    1522 PAT DORD REMOVED_DATE    1217 PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    1220 PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    1223 PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    1224 PAT MURJCOPIES TO  CAHILL TERESA M D  NWH RADIOLOGY DEPT  NEWTON  MA REMOVED_CASE_ID  617 243 6600 NEWTON CHEH EMILY M D  2000 WASHINGTON ST  NEWTON  MA REMOVED_CASE_ID  617 965 7800MARKERS  Breast Disease Related Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    1522 PAT DORDPROCEDURES  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  10 28 08 1218 PAT MURJ  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    1522 PAT DORD REMOVED_DATE    1218 PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    1224 PAT MURJTISSUES  Breast  needle biopsy   right Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    1522 PAT DORDFinal  ABBOTT TODD MD   REMOVED_DATE   10 28 08 1425  by MD ABBT MIHOK NICOLE MD        REMOVED_DATE   10 28 08 1430  by MD MIHN                                                                                             , 0.
