Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Specimen Type  Soft tissue debridement Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  REZA ASKARI M D  CASE  BS 09 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PATIENT  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME Resident  Scott Lovitch  M D   Ph D  Pathologist  George F Murphy  MD PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS  A  LEFT BREAST  TISSUE  Pan dermal and subcutaneous florid neutrophilic infiltrate  MSS and gram stains are negative   see COMMENT  COMMENT  Although it is difficult to exclude necrotizing fasciitis with certainty  the substantial pan dermal infiltrate by neutrophils with associated superficial ulceration in the absence of primary endothelial occlusive alterations and zonal necrosis would favor pyoderma gangrenosum  The extent of subcutaneous involvement is  however  somewhat unusual for this entity  although secondary involvement from the overlying dermis and nature of sampling  debridement of more advanced regions  may in part account for this finding   It is recommended that the final diagnostic assessment also include consideration of correlative clinical parameters  notably exclusion of an infectious cause  In addition  if at anytime the clinical parameters continue to raise the possibility of necrotizing fasciitis  as opposed to an atypically deep advanced manifestation of pyoderma gangrenosum   sampling of an early evolving lesion or lesion edge  as opposed to a debridement sampling  is suggested  Case referred by Surgical Pathology to Dermatopathology on REMOVED_DATE  and this diagnosis reflects this consultative review  CLINICAL DATA  History  NEC soft tissue infection  Operation  Washout debridement  left breast  Operative Findings  Not provided  Clinical Diagnosis  Necrotizing fascitis  TISSUE SUBMITTED  A 1  Left breast tissue GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received fresh  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tissue   and consists of an aggregate of irregular fragments of fibroadipose tissue  400 g  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  partially surfaced by tan pink skin  up to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension   The skin is diffusely devoid of epidermis  approximately 65  of the specimen   The specimen is serially sectioned to exhibit 100  homogenous yellow lobulated adipose tissue  The subcutaneous tissue directly underlying the skin exhibits diffuse green yellow discoloration  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Multi frags total  RSS  CASE NUMBER  REMOVED_CASE_ID  JC ajb By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated  of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es  related thereto  Final Diagnosis by George F Murphy MD  Electronically signed on Friday May 22  2009 at 02 15 20PM  report_end , 0.
