Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Specimen Type  Consult slides Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  DAVID A  SHERMAN M D  CASE  BS 05 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PATIENT  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME Resident  Eric J Burks  M D  Pathologist  Susan Lester  M D   Ph D  PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS  CONSULT SLIDES FROM EMERSON HOSPITAL  CONCORD  MA  RIGHT BREAST  EXCISION FOR  CHRONIC INFECTION  MASS LESION  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  9 12 2005   Granulomatous and suppurative inflammation and a pattern consistent with granulomatous lobular mastitis  see note   No vasculitis is seen  Special studies for organisms are negative  AFB  GMS  PAS  reviewed   Note  The histologic features of granulomatous inflammation centered on ducts and lobules and granulomas with clear centers  occasionally with neutrophils  are typical of granulomatous lobular mastitis  This is a disease of unknown cause that is essentially only observed in patients with a prior history of pregnancy  The extent of inflammation in this resection  with focal ulceration of the skin  largely obscures the classic distribution and is unusual  However  this may be due to the prior tru cut needle biopsy and skin biopsy  However  cultures for unusual organisms  e g  atypical mycobacteria and fungi  if the lesion recurs  are helpful to exclude an infectious etiology  CLINICAL DATA  History  Right breast chronic infection in a 39 year old woman with two children  Non smoker  Clinical Diagnosis  Granulomatous mastitis TISSUE SUBMITTED  Consult slides  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received from Emerson Hospital  Pathology Department  133 Old Road to Nine Acre Corner  Concord  MA REMOVED_CASE_ID  are ten  10  glass slides  The slides are labeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and sublabeled  B    C    H    H AFB    H GMS    H PAS    I  and  K  through  M   corresponding to A J  right breast excision for a mass  5 5 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm  K M  right breast excision  2 for a mass  3 5 x 3 x 3 cm  performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient s name  By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated  of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es  related thereto  Resident Review by Eric J Burks M D   on REMOVED_DATE  Final Diagnosis by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on 12 4 2005  report_end , 0.
