Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 58 CLINICAL DATA  Breast carcinoma by prior biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     RIGHT BREAST AND AXILLARY CONTENTS  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  8 CM IN DIAMETER  INVASIVE OF PECTORALIS MUSCLE  METASTATIC TO SIX OF SIX CONTIGUOUS INTRAMAMMARY LYMPH NODES  THE EXAMINED RESECTION MARGINS ARE NEGATIVE FOR TUMOR  2  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITHIN SIXTEEN OF TWENTY TWO AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  WITH EXTENSIVE EXTRACAPSULAR SPREAD ADJACENT TO SIX OF THESE POSITIVE NODES  NOTE  Although minor areas show tubular differentiation and are grade 1  the bulk of the tumor is grade 3  Central portions are scirrhous  Immunostains for estrogen and progesterone receptors will be performed and the results reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 09 09     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR C REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID AS REPORTED FOR IMPATH BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for CerB 2 Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 58 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  Right modified radical mastectomy   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm skin ellipse with a REMOVED_DATE cm well healed scar  Portions of muscle are attached on the posterior aspect  Directly beneath the scar is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm ill defined white firm mass that extends to REMOVED_DATE cm from the inked margin  extends into muscle  and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the overlying skin ellipse  The remainder of the parenchyma is unremarkable  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm axillary tail is attached  and contains multiple pink tan lymph nodes  the largest REMOVED_DATE cm  Section Code  A  closest margin of mass  B C  biopsy cavity  D H  representative sections of mass  I Q  lymph node dissection  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD                                                                                