Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID LUMPECTOMY Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  LESTER  SUSAN  M D  PH D  DIAGNOSIS  by LESTER SUSAN M D  PH D  LEFT BREAST LUMPECTOMY  WITH FSA   INFILTRATING AND IN SITU DUCTAL CARCINOMA  The invasive component  2 5 cm  is poorly differentiated  modified Bloom Richardson Grade III III   with extensive tumor necrosis  Invasive tumor is not present at the margin but is within REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral margin  The in situ component  solid and comedo type  high grade nuclear features  is present as multiple foci around the main tumor mass  ten of twelve slides  and is at or within REMOVED_DATE cm of the margin in four slides  3 and 7 deep  5 and 6 lateral   The infiltrating pattern of the invasive tumor makes it difficult to judge the extent of in situ carcinoma within it  No vascular invasion seen  Fat necrosis  history of prior needle biopsy   NOTE  Unusual features of this tumor are the very high grade  anaplastic  nuclei and the extensive necrosis  AXILLARY LYMPH NODE DISSECTION  Seventeen lymph nodes with no tumor seen  CLINICAL DATA  History  None given  Operation  Left breast  TISSUE SUBMITTED   1  left breast tissue  short stitch   superior medial  long stitch inferior    2  left axillary nodes  O R  CONSULTATION  LEFT BREAST LUMPECTOMY  FS A   Infiltrating ductal carcinoma  2 5 cm   extending within REMOVED_DATE cm of inked  lateral deep  margin  suspect in situ carcinoma at periphery of main mass  Gross specimen and frozen sections slides reviewed with Dr  Jacobsen  Tumor sent for ER PR and flow cytometry  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by KRAUS MADELEINE M D  Part one  received fresh  labeled with the patient s name and number  is a 5 x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm skin bearing  2 0 x REMOVED_DATE cm  fibrofatty tissue fragment with two orienting sutures attached  designated by surgeon as superior medial and inferior   At the center of the specimen  and grossly extending to within REMOVED_DATE  cm of the medial deep resection margins is a REMOVED_DATE cm well circumscribed firm nodule with gritty texture on cutting  A representative section of the tumor with deep resection margin is taken for frozen section  see above O R  consultation report   Immediately adjacent to the area of the long suture  identified by surgeon as inferior deep  is an area of firmness and hyperemia  No other abnormalities are identified  Part two   left axillary nodes   consists of a 7 x 4 x 3 cm mass of fibrofatty tissue within which approximately fourteen lymph nodes are identified  One of the lymph nodes contains a centrally located  white  REMOVED_DATE cm dot  and it is bisected and submitted entirely in the same cassette as a representative section of skin  Micro 1  frozen section remnant A  Micro REMOVED_DATE  deep resection margin  Micros REMOVED_DATE  lateral margin  Micro REMOVED_DATE  medial resection margin  Micro REMOVED_DATE  inferior resection margin  Micro REMOVED_DATE  superior resection margin  Micro 13  skin and lymph node with central white dot  Micro REMOVED_DATE  lymph nodes  Reports to  JACOBSEN  DAVID M D  SPECIMEN TYPE  LUMPECTOMY ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE  AXILLARY NODES  report_end , 0.
