led with the patient s name and unit number  Part A   Right breast tissue from localization   consists of one piece of breast tissue  5 0 cm from yellow to orange x REMOVED_DATE cm from green to red x REMOVED_DATE cm from blue to black   There is a wire within the center of this lesion and an accompanying report that reads   mass seen on ultrasound of specimen  no markers seen   The specimen comes previously inked by the surgeon  Orange is opposite yellow  blue is opposite of black and red is opposite of green  However  it is impossible for this specimen to be inked properly for right breast tissue  The surgeon was paged in order to resolve this discrepancy  However  she did not return the page  therefore one axis is incorrect  and it is impossible to determine which one  Subsequently we will refer to all margins according to the ink colors only  Of note the black surface is in a straight plane where the blue surface is convex  The specimen is cut along the plane of the wire through the orange yellow and red green surfaces and parallel to the blue and black surfaces  The specimen is cut into four slices with the wire being within slice 3  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Slice 1 blue margin  3 frags each  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Slice 2  green  yellow  and red margins  1 frag  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Slice 2  green  orange  and red margins  1 frag  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Slice 3  orange margin  1 frag  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Slice 3  yellow margin  1 frag  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Slice 3  green margin  1 frag  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Slice 3  red margin  1 frag  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Slice 4  black margin  3 frags each  ESS  Part B    1  Inferior margin   consists of one fragment of tissue  3 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7 cm   One surface is inked in green and the opposite surface is inked in black  There is an accompanying pink sheet report reading  no markers seen in either specimen   Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_I