Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  LESTER  SUSAN  M D  PH D  DIAGNOSIS  by LESTER SUSAN M D  PH D  LEFT BREAST  SENTINEL LYMPH NODE  INCLUDING FROZEN SECTION   One lymph node with no tumor seen  3 H E levels examined   LEFT BREAST  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  Atypical lobular hyperplasia  Epithelial hyperplasia  Radial sclerosing lesion  Apocrine cysts  Nipple and skin with no significant pathologic change  Note  There was an area of mammographic calcifications below the nipple which was identified by specimen radiography and extensively sampled  There are numerous calcifications present  associated with benign epithelium  No carcinoma is identified  ADDITIONAL INFERIOR MEDIAL  Fibroadipose tissue  Note  No breast epithelium is identified  CLINICAL DATA  History  Prior history of right breast carcinoma  Now with increasing sub  areolar calcifications of left breast  Operation  Sentinel node biopsy  left mastectomy  placement of left breast tissue expander  TISSUE SUBMITTED  1  Sentinel lymph node 2  Left mastectomy   short superior on skin margin  long lateral on axillary tail 3  Additional inferior medial O R  CONSULTATION  1  SENTINEL LYMPH NODE  FSA   Lymph node  no tumor present  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by LESTER SUSAN M D  PH D  The specimen is received fresh in three parts  labeled with the patient s name and unit number  The first part  labeled  Sentinel lymph node  1  consists of one fragment of adipose tissue  1 5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  containing a single REMOVED_DATE cm lymph node that is bisected and completely submitted for frozen section  Cass  1  Frozen section remnant  2 frags  ESS  The second part  labeled  left mastectomy  stitches mark short   superior on skin margin  long on axillary tail  is a simple mastectomy specimen  10 x 17 x 2 cm  335 grams  with a tan white skin ellipse  8 x 4 cm  with an everted normal appearing nipple  1 5 cm in diameter   One suture marks the superior portion of the skin ellipse  The other suture marks lateral tissue  Two wires exit from the skin ellipse   one marked with tape from the lateral edge of the areola  and one not marked with tape from inferior to the nipple  The specimen was radiographed in the radiology department by Dr  Darrell Smith  He placed two wires that bracket an area of calcifications deep to  and inferior to  the nipple  The specimen radiograph reveals the two wires and a diffuse area of calcifications over an area measuring approximately 3 cm  There is a 5 x 3 x 2 cm area of blue dome cysts and fibrous tissue just deep to the nipple and bracketed by the wires  No areas suspicious for invasive carcinoma are seen  No lymph nodes are seen in the lateral tissue marked by the suture after thinly sectioning and palpating the tissue  The remainder of the breast consists predominantly of adipose tissue with approximately 10  fibrous tissue with small cysts  The area bracketed by the wires is extensively sampled  approximately 80   from medial to lateral  Cass  2  Most medial portion of bracketed area  1 frag  RSS  Cass  3 4  Area of wire inferior to nipple  3 frags  RSS  Cass  5 6  Area between the wires  3 frags  RSS  Cass  7 8  Area of wire lateral to nipple  deep margin in  7  3 frags  RSS  Cass  9  Cross sections of nipple  3 frags  ESS  Cass  10  Base of nipple  1 frag  ESS and skin  1 frag  RSS  Cass  11  Upper inner quadrant  2 frags  RSS  Cass  12  Upper outer quadrant  2 frags  RSS  Cass  13  Lower inner quadrant  2 frags  RSS  Cass  14  Lower outer quadrant  2 frags  RSS  The third part  labeled  Additional inferior medial  consists of a single fragment of yellow adipose tissue with thin strands of fibrous tissue  6 5 x 3 7 x REMOVED_DATE cm  The entire specimen is examined microscopically  Cass  15 17  3 frags  ESS  Reports to  LESNIKOSKI  BETH ANN M D  SPECIMEN TYPE  SENTINEL LYMPH NODE ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST 