Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Specimen Type  Consult material Procedure Date  Ordering Provider  ANN H PARTRIDGE M D  CASE  BS 09 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PATIENT  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME Resident  Stephanie Schulte  M D  Pathologist  Susan Lester  M D   Ph D  PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS  CONSULT SLIDES AND PARAFFIN BLOCK FROM CONCORD HOSPITAL  DEPARTMENT OF PATHOLOGY  CONCORD  NH  RIGHT BREAST  EXCISION FOR A MASS  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_DATE    UNCLASSIFIED SPINDLE CELL SARCOMA  low to intermediate grade  possibly myofibroblastic in type  at least REMOVED_DATE cm  invading in breast parenchyma  see note   The tumor is paucicellular to moderately cellular  Frequent tumor cells show marked nuclear pleomorphism with large nucleoli  Rare mitoses are present  less than 1 per 10 HPF s   No necrosis is present  The tumor has an infiltrative border  The tumor is present at cauterized specimen edges  Immunohistochemical studies performed at Massachusetts General Hospital or Children s Hospital are reported to show the following results  Cytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 2 Negative Keratin Negative Epithelial membrane antigen Negative Muscle actin Positive  focal  weak  Smooth muscle actin Positive   focal Desmin Positive   focal Caldesmon Negative Calponin Positive   focal Vimentin Positive S 100 Negative REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Negative Immunohistochemical studies performed at BWH reveal the following findings for the tumor  Desmin Positive   focal Smooth muscle alpha actin Positive   focal REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Very focal  weak Cytokeratin PANK Negative  see note  Cytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Negative  see note  Cytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 2 Negative  see note  Note  The patient presented with a palpable breast mass at age 17  The excisional specimen was received in multiple fragments with nodular areas measuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm  This is also the largest size on the glass slides  The case was reviewed by Dr  Andrew Rosenberg at MGH  who diagnosed  myofibroblastic sarcoma  grade REMOVED_DATE    MGH REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The case was also seen by Dr  Antonio Perez Atayde at Children s Hospital  C 02 505  who diagnosed  spindle cell sarcoma  not otherwise specified   morphologically intermediate grade   The immunoperoxidase studies were said to  support a myofibroblastic nature   Repeat immunoperoxidase studies performed at BWH confirm the presence of muscle markers  Cytokeratin studies are also negative  However  an area of cauterized normal epithelial cells are also negative for cytokeratin  The normal cells have probably lost immunoreactivity due to the cauterization  The patient subsequently underwent a re excision which was reported to be free of tumor  Concord Hospital REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  reviewed as Children s Hospital C 02 513   The patient recently presented with a small palpable mass at the prior surgical scar  The excisional specimen revealed a small neuroma  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_CASE_ID   The neuroma is compared to the prior sarcoma  The neuroma does not resemble the prior sarcoma and is likely related to the prior surgical trauma  Dr  Jason Hornick also reviewed this case and concurs with the interpretation  CLINICAL DATA  History  17 year old woman with a palpable breast mass  Clinical Diagnosis  Consistent with sarcoma  favor myofibroblastic type  TISSUE SUBMITTED  Consult slides  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received from Concord Hospital  Pathology Department  250 Pleasant Street  Concord  MA REMOVED_CASE_ID  are fifteen  15  glass slides and a paraffin block  The slides and the paraffin block are labeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   the paraffin block is sublabeled  2   and the slides are sublabeled  FS    1    2  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    S 100    MUSCLE ACTIN    VIMENTIN    SM MUS ACTIN    EMA    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 3 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 22KER    KERATIN    CALDESMON    CALPONIN  and  DESMIN   corresponding to a right breast excision performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient s name  By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated  of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es  related thereto  Final Diagnosis by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on Wednesday REMOVED_MONTH 25  2009 at 04 14 12PM  report_end , 0.
