Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W O MARGINS Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  LESTER  SUSAN  M D  PH D  DIAGNOSIS  by LESTER SUSAN M D  PH D  LEFT BREAST BIOPSY  UPPER INNER QUADRANT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  cribiform type  low nuclear grade  within a fibroadenoma  size of fibroadenoma REMOVED_DATE cm   and focally in adjacent breast tissue  present in eight of eight sections  see note below   No necrosis or calcifications are associated with the carcinoma in situ  Hyalinized subcutaneous fibrosis  consistent with keloid  LEFT BREAST BIOPSY  UPPER OUTER QUADRANT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  cribiform type  low nuclear grade  within a fibroadenoma  size of fibroadenoma 3 cm  and focally in adjacent breat tissue  present in five of seven sections  see note   No necrosis or calcifications are associated with the carcinoma in situ  NOTE  Extensive cribiform ductal carcinoma in situ is present involving both fibroadenomas  Focal ductal carcinoma in situ is also present in adjacent breast tissue  although in most sections tissue outside the confines of the fibroadenomas is not present  Ductal carcinoma in situ is within REMOVED_DATE cm of the margin in all sections  Severe atypia approaching carcinoma in situ has been described in fibroadenomas in young women  Mies and Rosen  Am Surg Path 11 184  1987  and these women are reported to have an excellent prognosis during the interval of follow up  approximately 8 years   However  the proliferation seen in this patient is best classified as ductal carcinoma in situ due to its extent  atypia  and presence outside of the fibroadenomas  CLINICAL DATA  History  20 year old female with mass left breast  probable fibroadenomas  Operation  Excision of lesion upper inner quadrant  and excision of lesion upper outer quadrant  TISSUE SUBMITTED  Not stated   NOTE  The Form 86 states that the specimens are from the left breast  but the specimens are labelled right breast  Dr  Eberlein was contacted  and stated that tissue is from the left side   GROSS DESCRIPTION  by RUIZ ROBERT ERIC M D  PH D  The specimens are received fixed in two parts  each labelled with the patient s name and number  The first part  labeled   1   right breast tissue UIQ    but designated left  see above  consists of a tan white  rubbery  nodular tissue fragment  3 7 x REMOVED_DATE  x REMOVED_DATE cm   with a uniform  whorled texture on cross section  Also received is a grossly unremarkable tan skin ellipse  3 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm  incised to a depth of 1 1 cm   Micro  1 8  Left breast tissue  UIQ  ESS  multiple frags  8 cass  Micro  9  Skin left breast  upper inner quadrant  RSS  4 frags  The second part  labeled   2   right breast tissue UOQ    but designaated left  see above  is a rubbery  tan pink tissue fragment  3 x 3 x 2 cm   with a bulging whorled appearance on cut surface  There are no areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma  Micro  10 17  Left breast tissue  upper outer quadrant  ESS  9 frags  8 cass  Reports to  EBERLEIN  TIMOTHY  JOSEPH M D  SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST BIOPSY W O MARGINS  report_end , 1.
