Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Specimen Type  Breast core needle biopsy Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  EREN D YEH M D  CASE  BS 07 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PATIENT  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME Resident  Dominique P  Coco  M D  Pathologist  Susan Lester  M D   Ph D  PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  UPPER OUTER  14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR AN IRREGULAR REMOVED_DATE CM MASS  Fragments of a sclerosing lesion with atypical features  at least REMOVED_DATE cm  additional levels examined   Apocrine cysts  Epithelial hyperplasia  Note  The findings are most compatible with a complex sclerosing lesion with entrapped sclerosed glands  An immunoperoxidase study for cytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and p63 confirms the presence of myoepithelial cells in most areas  However  there are two small clusters of cells that do not show immunoreactivity  This lesion would be evaluated best after excision  CLINICAL DATA  HISTORY  35 year old female with R breast mass    CA  BREAST IMAGING FINDING  1  Right  5 mm  non palpable irregular mass  LOCATION  1  Right  upper outer TYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY  1  14G Ultrasound TISSUE SUBMITTED  1  14G Ultrasound 5   Pink cassette  GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received in formalin  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast pink   and contains a single pink cassette  Within the pink cassette  are multiple yellow tan fibroadipose tissue cores  1 5 x REMOVED_DATE  x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate   Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Multi frags  ESS  DFI mmm CASE NUMBER  REMOVED_CASE_ID By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated  of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es  related thereto  Final Diagnosis by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on 12 4 2007  report_end , 0.
Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 37 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  100   MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION AS MEASURED ON A GLASS SLIDE  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  There is no evidence of lymphatic or blood vascular invasion  The intra operative gross diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 09                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 14 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled with the patient s name  unit number only is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of dense breast with an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm firm nodule  within REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest inked surface  Submitted entirely in cassettes A through H with nodule in A and B  Resident  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  SUSPICIOUS LESION TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY   report_end , 1.
