Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  23 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  23 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 56 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISON BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  80   AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  SOLID  CRIBFORM AND CAMEDO TYPES  20    SEE NOTE  NOTE  Multiple foci of the atypical ductal hyperplasia and in situ carcinoma as well as one focus of invasive carcinoma are found at a distance from the main mass  The main tumor is present next to the inked resection margin  There is no definite lymphatic or vascular invasion seen  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 32                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 25 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast  is a 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 cm piece of fibrofatty breast tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm white tan  sclerotic mass which is located approximately REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest resection margin  The remaining parenchyma is fatty with firm white areas  A representative section of the mass is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  Representative sections of the tumor are submitted in A through D  and sections of the remaining breast tissue submitted E through J  Resident  STAMATINA KAPTAIN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA and FROZEN TISSUE IS SAVED  O R  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST MASS  RIGHT   report_end , 0.
