Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 36 CLINICAL DATA  66 year old female with extensive fungating right breast mass  also history of Crohn s disease with ascites                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     COLON  RESECTION  SEVERELY ACTIVE CHRONIC GRANULOMATOUS COLITIS  CONSISTENT WITH CROHN S COLITIS  WITH ULCERATION  FISTULA FORMATION  AND MULTIFOCAL TRANSMURAL NECROSIS   SEE NOTE   NOTE  The distal margin shows severely active colitis with ulceration  The proximal margin shows fibrosis and regressed Peyer s patches  There is no evidence of dysplasia  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSIES  INFILTRATING ADENOCARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 57 Staff Pathologist  Fiona M  Graeme Cook  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 07 18 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  colon   is an ileocolonic resection specimen  REMOVED_DATE cm in length with an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm omentum and a REMOVED_DATE cm length of distal ileum measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in circumference proximally and REMOVED_DATE cm in circumference distally  The serosal surface along the entire length of bowel is tan to brown and covered by indurated tan brown  hemorrhagic mesenteric fat  which creeps along the serosal surface in multiple areas and focally encases the segment of bowel  Approximately REMOVED_DATE cm from the distal resection margin are two serosal defects  measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension  surrounded by indurated hemorrhagic fat and lined by tan to brown fibrinous exudate  The surgeon states that multiple colonic perforations are present  now walled off by mesenteric fat  The segment of omentum is indurated  dark red to brown with a micronodular appearance  The segment of bowel is opened to reveal multiple regions where the mucosa is ulcerated  now lined by a tan to brown  focally green fibrinous exudate  surrounded by more preserved areas of mucosa resembling pseudopolyps  Towards the distal end of the specimen  the mucosa has a cobblestone appearance which extends to the distal resection margin  The region of the cecum and proximal ascending colon as well as the proximal resection margin appear spared of disease  In the region of ulcerative mucosa  the bowel wall appears markedly thickened measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in maximal thickness  The more preserved areas of mucosa are sectioned to reveal a maximal thickness measuring REMOVED_DATE cm  No appendix is identified  SEction Code  A  proximal resection margin B  distal resection margin C E  representative sections of serosal perforations surrounded by an indurated mesenteric fat F T  representative sections of diseased mucosa with cassettes  P  through  T  demonstrating the more cobblestone mucosa towards the distal end of the colon U  representative section of more normal appearing colonic mucosa V  representative section of indurated micronodular attached omentum  Received fresh labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  left breast biopsy   are multiple tan yellow soft tissue cores  measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in length and REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter  submitted entirely in cassette W  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  Bernard Ralph Aserkoff  M D  PART A  COLON PART B  BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSIES  report_end , 0.
