Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 22 CLINICAL DATA  Persistent right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY    INFILTRATING MAMMARY CARCINOMA  60    ADENOID CYSTIC TYPE  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM AN INKED SURFACE   SEE NOTE    INTRADUCTAL ADENOID CYSTIC CARCINOMA  40   PRESENT AT SEVERAL INKED SURFACES    INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  FOCAL    FIBROADENOMA  HYALINIZED  NOTE  The tumor is poorly differentiated  grade III III  utilizing the grading system of Ro et al  Hum  Path  1987  18 1276 81   Blood  vascular and lymphatic invasion is not identified  Histochemically the tumor demonstrates focal Alcian blue staining and PAS positive  diastase resistant staining in cylindromatous elements  The tumor demonstrates diffuse REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID immunoperoxidase staining and focal REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 3  CAM REMOVED_DATE  wide spectrum keratin  smooth muscle actin  EMA and vimentin staining consistent with adenoid cystic type  The tumor cells do not stain for chromogranin and muscle actin  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  06 MAY 94 at 17 20                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 MAY 94 at 08 49     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue with a palpable firm mass  The firm mass  which is composed of firm  irregular tan white tissue is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  and is REMOVED_DATE cm from an inked surface  Also present is a tan area that extends to an inked margin  Tumor is submitted in cassettes A through D  and all remaining tissue in cassettes E though J  Representative tumor sent for Estrogen receptor study  The frozen section is saved frozen  Resident  Rex Neal Smith  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Kathleen O Neil Smith  BUMS O R  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                          