Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W O MARGINS Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  WELCH  WILLIAM  ROBERT  M D  DIAGNOSIS  by WELCH WILLIAM ROBERT M D  SPECIMEN LABELED  RIGHT BREAST MASS   INCLUDING FROZEN SECTION   Atypical stromal proliferation  histologically benign  See note   The entire specimen was submitted for microscopical examination   SPECIMEN LABELED  SKIN TAG  LEFT BREAST   Acrochordon  NOTE  The tumor is characterized by florid proliferation of stromal cells with spindled  giant and bizarre multinucleate forms in a loose  somewhat myxoid  background  Mitoses are rare  less than 1 per 10 high power fields   Lobular ductal units within the tumor are not hyperplastic  There is no condensation of stromal cells around the epithelial units  Similar stromal changes  including loose myxoid perilobular stroma and isolated interlobular stromal giant cells  are present in adjacent breast tissue  The differential diagnosis includes fibroadenoma with bizarre stromal cells and low grade phyllodes tumor  The epithelial growth pattern is not characteristic of fibroadenoma  however  and distinctive features of phyllodes tumor  such as active mitotic rate  atypical mitoses  and foliated architecture  are likewise absent  We believe this lesion is a proliferation of atypical stromal cells  Margins could not be evaluated  due to prior incision   The presence of tumor cells at the edges of some microscopic sections and the stromal changes in adjacent breast  suggesting progressive recruitment  make re excision advisable  CLINICAL DATA  History  Mass right breast  Skin tag left nipple  Operation  Excision right breast mass  removal skin tag left nipple  Clinical Diagnosis  Right breast mass  skin tag left nipple  TISSUE SUBMITTED  1  Right breast mass  2  Left skin tag nipple  O R  CONSULTATION  Right breast mass  Bizarre cellular myxoid stromal proliferation  malignancy  including phyllodes tumor  cannot be excluded   Tissue put in for electron microscopy  on hold   GROSS DESCRIPTION  by HEVNER ROBERT FRANCIS M D  PH D  The specimen is received in formalin  in two parts  each labeled with the patient s name and unit number  The first part  labeled  right breast mass   consists of a single fragment of tan yellow  fibrofatty tissue  2 8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm   with a well circumscribed  firm  tan white nodule  1 3 cm  with hemorrhagic appearing spots  The specimen has been partially cut into prior to receiving in the cutting room and is therefore not inked  A representative section of the nodule is submitted for frozen section A  the frozen block is saved for possible further immunoperoxidase  ERICA  or other studies  A representative sample of the nodule is submitted for electron microscopy  hold   Micros REMOVED_DATE   right breast biopsy  ESS  12 fragments  4 cassettes The second part  labeled  skin tag left breast   consists of a single tiny fragment of tan  soft tissue  0 2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm   Micro 5   skin tag left nipple  1 fragment  1 cassette Reports to  FEDERSCHNEIDER  JEROME  MILES M D  SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST BIOPSY W O MARGINS  report_end , 0.
