roximately 5 cm  inferior to the nipple  there is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm  area of scar on the skin surface  Otherwise  the nipple and surrounding skin surface are grossly unremarkable  On the deep surface  there is a smooth surface of adipose tissue with no gross evidence of tumor seen  In the area deep to the location of the skin scar  the deep surface has a somewhat indurated feel and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  area of apparent skeletal muscle fibers  The margins throughout are inked  Cross sectioning demonstrates areas of fibrosis and coarse calcification in the fibroadipose tissue underlying the skin scar as well as a focal area of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm  cavity  Aside from the rubbery fibrosis and calcification  no discrete mass lesion is seen in this area or in the area surrounding this area  remote scar and calcification  Away from this area  the remainder of the parenchyma is primarily yellow lobulated adipose tissue with thin strands of white tan fibrous tissue and focal areas of rubbery white fibrous tissue but with no grossly suspicious areas seen  Multiple sections through the skin and underlying breast tissue of the nipple are made with no gross evidence of lesions seen  Section code  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   lateral aspect REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   lateral aspect of superior portion REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   central portion REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   superior medial portion REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   medial aspect REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   representative sections from around prior excision site and adjacent to calcified areas REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   representative sections after decalcification of hard calcified areas  including deep margin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   nipple REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   deep to nipple Specimen B labeled  inferior margin  left breast  left   is received in formalin and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  portion of fibroadipose tissue with focal rubbery firm areas  Sectioning demonstrates no grossly suspicious areas  It is serially submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  8 agg  all  Specimen C labeled  right breast  stitch at 12 o clock  is received fresh and is examined in the Operating Room  It consists of a 605 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 3 cm  simple mastectomy specimen marked at one aspect  clinically oriented as superior of the right breast and having a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  skin ellipse with an unremarkable REMOVED_DATE cm  in diameter nipple on the superficial surface  The deep surface is a smooth flat portion of fibroadipose tissue with no gross lesions seen  The margins throughout are inked  Representative sections of bread loaf sectioning across the entire specimen fresh in the Operating Room demonstrates mostly yellow lobulated adipose tissue with thin strands of white tan fibrous tissue  focal rubbery  firm areas of fibrous tissue and no gross evidence of tumor mass seen  in the area immediately deep to the nipple  some of the transected ducts appear dilated and contain a soft  whitish tan material  A representative section of this area deep to the nipple is submitted for frozen section and resubmitted in CF  No other areas similar to this are seen away from the area of the nipple  Section code  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   lateral REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   superior lateral portion REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   inferior lateral REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   nipple REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   representative area deep to nipple REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   central portion REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   superior medial portion REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   inferior medial portion REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   medial portion Specimen D labeled  right chest wall skin  is received in formalin and consists of two irregular portions of skin  the larger REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm   REMOVED_DATE cm  deep  It is roughly triangular shaped  The second is REMOVED_DATE cm  long  REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm  in width and REMOVED_DATE cm  deep  Slight scar like irregularity is seen on some of the skin surface  No evidence of suspicious lesions are seen  Sections from the larger portion are submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  from the second portion  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 agg  Specimen E labeled  left mid chest wall skin  suture medial  is received fresh and consists of a 7 x REMOVED_DATE cm  ellipse of skin  REMOVED_DATE cm  deep and having a suture in the mid portion of one side  clinically designated as medial and arbitrarily designated as 12 o clock  The margins throughout are inked black  Located near the side opposite from the suture  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  slightly pigmented area  No suspicious areas are seen on sectioning  Representative sections are submitted  6X  Section code  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   superior end REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   medial half  from superior to inferior REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   lateral half  from superior to inferior including entirety of pigmented area REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   inferior end Specimen F labeled  left lateral chest wall skin  suture lateral  is received fresh and consists of an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm  in width x REMOVED_DATE cm  in depth slightly irregularly shaped excision of skin which is marked with a suture in the mid portion of one aspect  This is designated as lateral  At the inferior aspect of this  there is a slight thickening of the skin surface on the inferior medial aspect  The margins are inked throughout  No suspicious areas are seen on the cut surface  Representative sections are submitted  Section code  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   superior end REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   mid portion REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   medial side of mid to inferior portion REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   lateral side of mid to inferior portion REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   inferior aspect Dictated by  DDK____ signature on file ____DANIEL D  KOELLIKER  M D  REMOVED_DATE   Final   report_end , 0.
