Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Specimen Type  Breast core needle biopsy Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  EVA C  GOMBOS M D  CASE  BS 09 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PATIENT  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME Resident  Mariana A  Stoleru  M D  Pathologist  Susan Lester  M D   Ph D  PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  CENTRAL LOWER  14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A PALPABLE PAINFUL GREATER THAN 6 CM IRREGULAR MASS  Breast tissue with a mixed inflammatory infiltrate consisting of neutrophils  eosinophils  plasma cells  and scattered giant cells  predominantly centered around lobules  see note   Poorly formed granulomas are present adjacent to lobules  There are empty spaces in the areas of inflammation lined by neutrophils  Gram positive bacilli are present on the Gram stain and on the silver stain  MSS   No fungal organisms or acid fast bacilli are seen  MSS and AFB stains   Note  The biopsy shows features characteristic of granulomatous lobular mastitis  However  the presence of bacterial forms suggests that there is also a bacterial infection  Anaerobic bacteria should be considered  Cultures would be helpful to better evaluate an infectious process  This case was also reviewed by Dr  Dan Milner  CLINICAL DATA  HISTORY  45 year old woman with history of minor trauma to the breast by a child  with pain but without bruising  The breast became painful and she was diagnosed with fat necrosis and infection on a trip to Mexico and treated with clindamycin  She now has a painful palpable mass  MRI shows a 9 x 4 x 4 cm area of heterogeneous enhancement  BREAST IMAGING FINDING  1  Left  over 6 cm  palpable and irregular mass  LOCATION  1  Left  Central Lower TYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY  1  14 G Ultrasound TISSUE SUBMITTED  1  14 G Ultrasound 10 55 AM   Green cassette  GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received in formalin  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and consists of multiple tan white to tan y