ed into four equal parts  4X all  Specimen B labeled  excision  right breast  is received in formalin  On the anterior surface is a thin ellipse of skin REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  There is a linear scar running through the skin  On the superior surface is a short green surface and on the lateral surface is a long green suture  On the inferior portion of the specimen  there is some bluish discoloration of the adipose tissue  The superior edge is inked with blue ink  The remainder of the specimen is inked with black ink  The cut surface of the superior margin shows recent focal hemorrhage and yellowish necrosis of fat  approximately REMOVED_DATE 7 cm  in area  near the superior margin  All remaining breast tissue shows focally indurated and yellowish parenchyma  The following sections are submitted  Section code  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   superior margin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   remaining tissue  medial to lateral sections  sequentially Specimen CF labeled  inferior margin  separate for frozen section  consists of a semicircular fragment of tissue held together by a small area  Each piece is 1 2 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm  It consists of greyish fibrocollagenous tissue and some adipose tissue  The outer edge is inked with black ink  1X all  Specimen C labeled  separate inferior margin  non frozen  consists of the remainder of the specimen 2 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm  The outer edge is inked with black ink  The inner edge is reddish and somewhat granular  It is divided into four equal parts  4X all  Dictated by  DJF____ signature on file ____MICHAEL J  ROSS  M D  REMOVED_DATE   Final  ____ signature on file ____DENNIS J  FEEN  M D  REMOVED_DATE   Final   report_end , 0.
Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Amend Addenda Type  Surgical Pathology Specimen Type  Breast core needle biopsy Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  MEHRA GOLSHAN M D  CASE  BS 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PATIENT  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME            Addended Report             Resident  Jane E Brock  M B   B S   Ph D  Pathologist  Scott J Rodig  M D   Ph D  PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  MASS  CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY  Sections show a densely fibrotic breast parenchyma with a mainly periductal dense lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate composed predominantly of small sized lymphocytes with regular nuclei  indistinct nucleoli and scant cytoplasm  Admixed  there are scattered intermediate sized lymphocytes and plasma cells  The lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate focally infiltrates into adjacent fibrotic tissue and the adjacent adipose tissue  Immunoperoxidase studies performed on paraffin sections reveal a mixed population of REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  T cells and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  B cells  T cells predominate within epithelial structures  Kappa and lambda immunoglobulin light chain stains reveal a polytypic population of plasma cells in the infiltrate  High background levels preclude optimal evaluation of REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID however it generally shows the T lymphocyte distribution  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID stains rare lymphoid cells  and the REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID staining pattern is similar to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  T cell staining pattern  Note  The overall findings are of a PROMINENT LYMPHOID INFILTRATE  which by immunophenotypic studies  is comprised of a mixture of T and B cells without overt phenotypic abnormality  Despite the density of the infiltrate  definitive features of involvement by a lymphoproliferative disorder are not seen  To further characterize this lesion  paraffin embedded tissue will be submitted for B and T cell gene rearrangement studies  the results of which will be reported in an addendum  CLINICAL DATA  History  Right breast mass  history of incisional biopsy x2  showing reactive changes on REMOVED_DATE  Operation  Right breast core biopsy Clinical Diagnosis  Right breast mass TISSUE SUBMITTED  Unspecified GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received in formalin  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  right breast core   and consists of cores of fibroadipose tissue  1 5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate   Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  mult frags  ESS Db jl By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated  of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es  related thereto  Resident Review by Jane E Brock M B   B S   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE  Final Diagnosis by Scott J Rodig M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on 1 17 2006 SURGICAL ADDENDUM  At the request of Dr  Sonali Desai  this case is reviewed again by Dr  Susan Lester and Dr  Jason Hornick  Immunohistochemical studies are performed for IgG  plasma cell  and IgREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  The area of the biopsy with an chronic inflammatory infiltrate is no longer present on the deeper levels used for the immunohistochemical studies  Therefore  these studies are noncontributory  The final diagnosis is unchanged  Addendum  1 by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 15  2009 at 04 17 51PM  report_end , 0.
