ing radiograph demonstrating the area localized by the wire  On the superior side of the specimen towards the anterior portion there are multiple tan granules of foreign material  likely consistent with gel foam that is injected by a surgeon to mark prior biopsy sites  The specimen was inked by pathology according to the pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins  posterior black  anterior blue  superior red  inferior green  lateral yellow  medial orange  The specimen is largely composed of fibrous tissue with no discrete masses  The specimen is sectioned serially from anterior to deep margin and entirely submitted  Note  the wire localizes an area in the most anterior aspect of the specimen  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  anterior most portion of the specimen containing the area localized by the wire  1 frag in each  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remainder of the specimen  serially sectioned  REMOVED_DATE fags in each  ESS  Part B is labeled   2   left breast wire loc biopsy   and consists of a breast excision specimen  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  The specimen is oriented by the surgeon  such that the short stitch indicates the superior margin  and the long stitch indicates the lateral margin  The specimen is inked by pathology according to the pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins  posterior black  anterior blue  superior red  inferior green  lateral yellow  medial orange  There is a wire in the specimen  as well as an accompanying radiograph  The wire localizes to a medial portion of the specimen  The specimen is sectioned from medial to lateral  The specimen is composed of fibroadipose tissue with no discrete nodules or masses  There is a white foreign material present in the posterior lateral portion of the specimen  likely consistent with gel foam injected into a prior biopsy site  The specimen is entirely submitted as follows  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  medial most section  1 frag  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID