Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 08 CLINICAL DATA  Mammographic density  rule out lymphoma vs  breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3 OF 3  SEE NOTE   THE FROZEN SECTION LAB GROSS DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  The tumor is composed only of infiltrating component  It measures REMOVED_DATE cm in largest diameter  measured from slides  and extends to the inked resection margin over a broad front  Neither vascular nor lymphatic invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 43                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 07 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled with the patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm piece of breast with localizing wire and X ray  Inked and sectined to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm well circumscribed firm  tan pink mass with mildly fleshy cut surface with foci of hemorrhage and more yellow areas  The lesion is grossly abutting the inked surface  A representative section is frozen as FX  1 and saved frozen and sent to Cox 5  The remainder is submitted from A E and representative sections of the rest in H J  Resident  ESTHER OLIVA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST  RIGHT   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Max L  Goodman  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   report_end , 0.
