Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 28 CLINICAL DATA  Huge mass  right mass  large axillary nodes                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  NEEDLE BIOPSY   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 15 28                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16 41 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received labeled with the patient s name and unit number only  are fragments of soft  tan pink tissue  The largest measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  incised and all the specimens are submitted in cassette labeled A  Gross Description by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  David William Rattner  M D  PART   BREAST  NEEDLE BIOPSY  RIGHT   report_end , 0.
