Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Specimen Type  Cyst  other  non neoplastic Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  MEHRA GOLSHAN M D  CASE  BS 09 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PATIENT  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME Resident  Matthew D  Stachler  M D   Ph D  Pathologist  Jacqueline M William  M D   Ph D  PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  CYST EXCISION  Benign ductal cyst  RIGHT BREAST  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A PALPABLE MASS  PHYLLODES TUMOR  low grade  REMOVED_DATE cm  see note   The stroma is moderately cellular with moderate nuclear atypia  Mitoses are present  focally up to 1 per 10 high power fields   Mild stromal overgrowth is present  The tumor focally infiltrates into the adjacent breast tissue  The tumor is present at the anterior margin    REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior and medial margins  and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin  The tumor is   REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin  The superior margin is not well seen  Immunohistochemical studies are performed with the following results for lesional cells  Smooth muscle myosin heavy chain POSITIVE Cytokeratin  PANK  NEGATIVE REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE NOTE  The stromal cells have an unusual myofibroblastic appearance with both spindle and epithelial morphologies  Immunohistochemical studies support that these are myofibroblasts and not of epithelial  myoepithelial  or vascular origin  The differential diagnosis includes a fibroadenoma extensively involved by pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia  The presence of occasional mitoses and nuclear atypia favor classification as a phyllodes tumor  This case was also reviewed by Dr  Susan Lester  RIGHT BREAST  WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS AND A CLIP  Benign breast tissue with columnar cell change and pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia  PASH   NOTE  The patient underwent a prior core needle biopsy for a REMOVED_DATE cm irregular mass and the biopsy showed PASH  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   PASH is again present in this excisional biopsy  Although biopsy site changes are not seen  there has been a long interval since the prior biopsy  The clip at the biopsy site was present  There is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the entire specimen  including margins  This case was also reviewed by Dr  Susan Lester  The immunoperoxidase  immunofluorescence and in situ hybridization tests performed at Brigham and Women s Hospital were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the Department of Pathology at BWH  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  CLINICAL DATA  History  25 year old with right breast fibroepithelial lesion and right breast pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia  S P core biopsy  Right breast mole  Operation  1  Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy  2  Right breast biopsy  Operative Findings  Not provided  Clinical Diagnosis  1  Right breast mass fibroepithelial lesion 2  Right breast mole  TISSUE SUBMITTED  A 1  Right breast cyst excision  B 2  Right breast excisional biopsy   short suture superior  long lateral  C 3  Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy   short suture superior  long lateral  mammo   RADIOLOGY  Specimen  3   specimen x ray shows clip and mass and intact wire  Habgo  GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received fresh  in three parts  each labeled with the patient s name and unit number  Part A  labeled   1  Right breast cyst excision   consists of a single irregular red brown fragment of soft tissue  0 6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm   The entire specimen is submitted for histologic evaluation  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Entire specimen  1 frag  ESS  Part B  labeled   2  Right breast excisional biopsy short suture superior long lateral   consists of a tan yellow firm lobulated fragment of