Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT   BREAST Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  LESTER  SUSAN  M D  PH D  DIAGNOSIS  by LESTER SUSAN M D  PH D  CONSULT SLIDES AND PARAFFIN BLOCK FROM CONCORD HOSPITAL  CONCORD  NH  RIGHT BREAST  1 00  STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_DATE    INVASIVE POORLY DIFFERENTIATED CARCINOMA  measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size  No carcinoma in situ is seen  No lymphovascular invasion is seen  Immunoperoxidase studies are performed with the following results  not reviewed   Keratin cocktail POSITIVE Leukocyte common antigen NEGATIVE Estrogen receptor NEGATIVE Progesterone receptor NEGATIVE REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu NEGATIVE  0  Note  The presence of cytokeratin immunoreactivity confirms the diagnosis of carcinoma  The carcinoma consists of cells with large pleomorphic nuclei growing in a syncytial pattern  surrounded by a prominent lymphocytic infiltrate  If the carcinoma was a well circumscribed mass  these findings would support a diagnosis of MEDULLARY CARCINOMA  The carcinoma appears to be within breast parenchyma and does not appear to be metastatic carcinoma to an intramammary lymph node  RIGHT BREAST  EXCISION  AND AXILLARY LYMPH NODE DISSECTION  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_DATE    Biopsy site with repair reaction  Epithelial hyperplasia  Apocrine cysts  METASTATIC CARCINOMA to one of twelve lymph nodes  The metastatic deposit measures REMOVED_DATE cm  No extranodal invasion is seen  Immunoperoxidase studies performed at BWH on the lymph node metastasis reveals the following  Cytokeratin  PANK  POSITIVE Estrogen receptor NEGATIVE Progesterone receptor NEGATIVE REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu NEGATIVE  0  Note  This carcinoma would be classified as AJCC REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDbiv MX  CLINICAL DATA  History  None given  Clinical Diagnosis  Right breast cancer  TISSUE SUBMITTED  Consult slides  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by BROWNE TARA JANE MB BCH BAO Received from Concord Hospital  250 Pleasant Street  Concord  NH REMOVED_CASE_ID are forty eight slides and one paraffin block  One slide is labeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and sublabeled  4   corresponding to a right breast stereotactic needle biopsy at 1 o clock  received on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient s name  Forty seven are labeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and sublabeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  to  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   including two levels on REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  corresponding to A  right breast lumpectomy  9 8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm   B  right breast margin  3 6 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6 cm   and C  right axillary lymph nodes  received on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient s name  The block is labeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   and sublabeled  C  and corresponds to the lymph node with metastastic carcinoma  The block is recut for immunoperoxidase studies  Reports to  LIGIBEL  JENNIFER  A  M D  SPECIMEN TYPE  OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT   BREAST ADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE  OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT   BREAST  report_end , 0.
Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  12 MAY 93 ACCESSIONED ON  12 MAY 93 at 15 40 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  BIOPSY   INFILTRATING AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor grows with an unusual pattern that makes it difficult to determine the proportions of in situ and invasive carcinoma  Blood vessel or lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The tumor shows staining for chromogranin and synaptophysin  which indicates neuroendocrine differentiation  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 MAY 93 at 16 49                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 MAY 93 at 13 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled with the patient s name  is a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter  irregularly shaped  firm  tan lesion abutting an inked margin  A representative section is frozen as Frozen Section  1 and saved frozen  The lesion is too small for biochemical estrogen receptor study  The remainder is submitted entirely in B through E  Resident  George O  Kucyj  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  BREAST LEFT   BIOPSY  CARCINOMA  PROBABLY INFILTRATING  AWAIT PERMANENTS   O R  Resident  Jo Ann E  Haney  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS  report_end , 0.
