tronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 07  2009 at 12 23 32PM SURGICAL ADDENDUM  4 07 09   Immunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the following results for invasive carcinoma  block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Estrogen receptor NEGATIVE Progesterone receptor NEGATIVE REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu  c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  NEGATIVE  1   Note  Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen and progesterone receptors  Immunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following criteria  Hormone receptor analysis  positive  10  of nuclei immunoreactive positive   low   0      10  of nuclei immunoreactive negative 0  of nuclei immunoreactive The lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet been determined  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu analysis  Negative  0   No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells  Negative  1    Faint weak immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells but only a portion of the membrane is positive  Equivocal  2   Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells  Positive  3   Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in  30  of tumor cells  Cytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result  External controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity  Some of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational use only  Addendum  1 by Deborah A Dillon M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 07  2009 at 05 19 59PM SURGICAL ADDENDUM  5 4 09   Immunohistochemistry for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is negative in the tumor cells  supporting the above diagnosis  Addendum  2 by Deborah A Dillon M D   Electronically signed on Monday May 04  2009 at 11 40 40AM  report_end , 1.
