Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Amend Addenda Type  Surgical Pathology Specimen Type  Breast  excisional tissue without margins Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  MEHRA GOLSHAN M D  CASE  BS 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PATIENT  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME            Addended Report             Resident  Michael H Roh  M D   Ph D   Jacqueline M William  M D   Ph D  Pathologist  Geraldine S Pinkus  M D  PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS  A  RIGHT BREAST MRI LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  DEEP RING ENHANCING LESION   Breast tissue with a focus  2 5 cm  of fat necrosis  dense fibrosis  histiocytic infiltrates and nodular lymphoid aggregates  see note  The lymphoid aggregates are composed primarily of small lymphocytes with condensed chromatin  indistinct nucleoli and scant cytoplasm  Admixed larger lymphocytes with vesicular chromatin  distinct nucleoli and moderate amounts of cytoplasm are also present  Scattered plasma cells are seen  Immunohistochemical studies performed on paraffin sections reveal that the lymphoid aggregates are composed of a mixture of REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID positive B lymphocytes and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID positive T lymphocytes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is noted for the T cells and possibly a subset of B cells  The plasma cells are polytypic for kappa and lambda light chain expression  Kappa and lambda light chain studies are difficult to evaluate for the B lymphocytes  NOTE  The overall findings are most suggestive of a reactive process  possibly related to the patient s prior surgical procedures  However  given the exuberance of the response  molecular studies will be performed to evaluate the process further  the results of which will be reported separately  B  RIGHT BREAST  MRI LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  UPPER OUTER QUADRANT  Breast tissue with dense fibrosis  foreign body giant cell reaction to polarizable material  hemosiderin laden macrophages  and lymphoid aggregates  see part A for further description   NOTE  This case was also reviewed by Dr  Michelle Hirsch of the Surgical Pathology service  Clinical  62 year old female with discoid lupus and four abnormally enhancing areas in the right breast  S P core biopsies and lumpectomy for fibroadenoma s   CLINICAL DATA  History  Right abnormal breast MRI x2 lesions  axillary adenopathy  First lesion  ring enhancing deep central breast  and second lesion  upper outer quadrant  Operation  1  Right breast MRI localized excisional biopsy  deep ring enhancing lesion  2  Right breast MRI localized excisional biopsy  upper outer quadrant  Clinical Diagnosis  Right breast  abnormal MRI x2 lesions  TISSUE SUBMITTED  A 1  Right breast MRI localized excisional biopsy  ring enhancing lesion  deep central breast  short suture superior  long lateral    mammo  B 2  Right breast MRI localized excisional biopsy  upper outer quadrant  short suture superior  long lateral    mammo RADIOLOGY  Specimen 1  mass   wire in specimen  Specimen 2  mass   wire in specimen  OR called SR  GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received fresh  in two parts  each labeled with the patient s name and unit number  Part A  labeled   1  Right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of fibroadipose tissue  oriented by sutures designating superior  short suture  and lateral  long suture   The specimen is received with a radiograph demonstrating the localizing wire in place within the specimen adjacent to an ill defined mass at the medial pole of the specimen  Sectioning demonstrates an ill defined  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  firm tan yellow  centrally hemorrhagic mass at the medial pole  abutting the medial  anterior  and superior margins  and within REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest posterior margin  REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest inferior margin  and greater than 3 cm from the closest lateral margin  The remaining specimen is predominantly adipose tissue  at least 85    without additional masses  lesions  or other abnormalities  grossly  The entire area of interest is submitted sequentially from medial to lateral  Approximately 20  of the specimen has been submitted  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Entire lesion  sequentially from medial to lateral  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is closest lateral margin   multi frags  ESS  Part B  labeled   2  Right breast MRI localized excisional biopsy  upper outer quadrant  short suture superior  long suture lateral    is a REMOVED_DATE x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of fibroadipose tissue  oriented by sutures designating superior  short suture  and lateral  long suture  margins  The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins  posterior black  anterior blue  superior red  inferior green  lateral yellow  medial orange  A truncated localizing wire enters the specimen s lateral aspect and exits the anterior inferior surface  The specimen is received with a radiograph demonstrating the localizing wire in place within the specimen adjacent to an ill defined lesion  Sectioning demonstrates a palpably firm  REMOVED_DATE cm  tan yellow nodule in this area  REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest inferior margin  REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest anterior margin  REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest posterior margin  REMOVED_DATE  cm from the closest superior margin  REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest lateral margin  and remote  greater than 2 cm  from the closest medial margin  The remaining specimen is predominantly is soft  lobulated  tan yellow adipose tissue  60   with a focus of firm  dense fibrous tissue  1 8 cm in greatest dimension   superiorly  The entire specimen is submitted  sequentially from lateral to medial  nodule and surrounding tissue in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  dense fibrous tissue in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Entire specimen  sequentially from lateral to medial  multi frags  ESS  DB ajb By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated  of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es  related thereto  Final Diagnosis by Geraldine S Pinkus M D   Electronically signed on 7 21 2006 SURGICAL ADDENDUM   added by Dr  G  Pinkus  REMOVED_DATE   Following a recent discussion with Dr  Alyssa Johnsen who inquired whether the findings might reflect lupus profundus  the slides were further reviewed at the Dermatopathology consensus conference  The staff concurred that while some of the features are suggestive of lupus profundus  lupus panniculitis   diagnostic features of this disorder are not seen  Molecular genetic studies which were performed on the tissue  see BL 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BL 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and BL 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  did not demonstrate a definitive clonal B cell population  Clinical correlation advised for further evaluation  Addendum  1 by Geraldine S Pinkus M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE   report_end , 0.
