Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 29 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   LEFT BREAST  NIPPLE BIOPSY    INVASIVE MAMMARY CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT AT AN INKED MARGIN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The limited amount of tumor in the biopsy precludes an accurate assessment of the type  ductal vs lobular  of mammary carcinoma  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not seen  There is no evidence of Paget s  BREAST   LEFT  BREAST TISSUE    BIOPSY  BREAST PARENCHYMA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 17                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 04 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled with the patient s name and unit number  in two parts  Labeled  Left breast nipple biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm pink soft tissue fragment  grossly unremarkable on sectioning and submitted entirely in cassette A  Labeled  Left breast tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm yellow pink soft adipose tissue with two firm white nodules REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension  Inked and sectioned and submitted entirely in cassette B  Resident  GARY LETTS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DX  NO SUSPICIOUS LESION LARGE ENOUGH TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  STUART HOUSER  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART A  BREAST NIPPLE BIOPSY  LEFT  PART B  BREAST  LEFT   report_end , 1.
