Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT   BREAST Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  LESTER  SUSAN  M D  PH D  DIAGNOSIS  by LESTER SUSAN M D  PH D  CONSULT SLIDES FROM HARVARD VANGUARD MEDICAL ASSOCIATES  BOSTON  MA  RIGHT BREAST  10 00  ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A NODULE  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_DATE    INVASIVE POORLY DIFFERENTIATED CARCINOMA  measuring at least 1 cm in size  see note   Lymphovascular invasion is present  A definite in situ component is not seen  Immunoperoxidase studies were performed by the original institution with the following results  reviewed   Estrogen receptor POSITIVE Progesterone receptor POSITIVE REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu NEGATIVE  1   CEA NEGATIVE GCDFP 15 NEGATIVE REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE Calponin NEGATIVE  for myoepithelial cells in tumor  Smooth muscle alpha actin NEGATIVE  for myoepithelial cells in tumor  Note  The carcinoma is histologically similar to the patient s poorly differentiated papillary serous adenocarcinoma  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID has been reported to be present in the majority of ovarian serous carcinomas  In one report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID was absent in 25 studied breast carcinomas  Therefore  this finding is more supportive of a metastatic origin for the current carcinoma  However  this finding is not considered definitive in the absence of additional supportive studies  CLINICAL DATA  History  None given  TISSUE SUBMITTED  Consult slides GROSS DESCRIPTION  by BROWNE TARA JANE MB BCH BAO Received from Harvard Vanguard Medical Associates  120 Brookline Ave  Boston  MA REMOVED_CASE_ID are ten  10  slides labeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and sublabeled  A REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    A ER m   A PR    A REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    A CEA    A SMA    A Calponin    A REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID monoclonal    A GCDFP   and  B REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   corresponding to an ultrasound guided core needle biopsy  10 o clock