Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  25 AUG 93 ACCESSIONED ON  25 AUG 93 at 13 54 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE    95   EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF INKED RESECTION MARGIN  AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA   5    SEE NOTE  2  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA  FOCAL  NOTE  The infiltrating carcinoma measures REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension  No vascular invasion is present Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Christophe Girardet  M D  Signed On  27 AUG 93 at 18 54                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 AUG 93 at 15 41 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm yellow  fibrofatty tissue fragment with superior thickening and accompanying x ray  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter thickened area with gray center and tan radiation  Representative sections of lesion frozen as frozen section  1 and  2  The remainder of the lesion submitted in cassettes A through C  and remainder of the specimen in cassettes D through O  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   BREAST LEFT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART   LEFT BREAST  report_end , 0.
