Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 09 34 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE    100  INFILTRATIVE   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor is present in 17 of 19 blocks and is present at the inked margin in many sections  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is recognized  The diffuseness of the tumor in the entire biopsy specimen indicates a large primary lesion of at least several centimeters in diameter  Frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 22                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT  EXCISION  BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   6   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean REMOVED_DATE   and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 00     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726 8865  estrogen receptor  Negative  progesterone receptor  Negative  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 38     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FROZEN TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining for estrogen receptor protein of 100 unfixed breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining for progesterone receptor protein of 50 breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Seventy three percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 91  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 17     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   RIGHT  EXCISION   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   6   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 463 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean REMOVED_DATE   and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 00     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     THIS ADDENDUM HAS BEEN DELETED FOR THIS REPORT GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the frozen section lab  labeled with the patient s name  number and  right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of fibrofatty breast parenchyma  inked and sectioned to reveal multiple white  rubbery foci and one slightly tan  gritty focus  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 _ cm which abuts the closest margin  Representative piece of gritty focus frozen as frozen section  1 and kept frozen  Estrogen receptors taken and specimen sent for BRDU  The remainder of tissue submitted in cassettes A S  Resident  Timothy R  Quinn  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  RIGHT BREAST MASS   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Jacqueline Haas  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS  report_end , 0.
