Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 17 CLINICAL DATA  Status post right mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  1 0 CM   GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SEE NOTE  2  MICROCALCIFICATION  NOTE  Greater than 95 per cent of the tumor is infiltrating  foci of in situ carcinoma apart from the main tumor are not identified  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is seen  The inked margins are negative for tumor  The gross intraoperative impression is confirmed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 17 22                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 12 05 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a 6 x 3 x 2 cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with accompanying x ray and wire in place  Specimen inked and bisected to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm firm  gray nodule suspcious for carcinoma  Surrounded by fat  not present at margin  Nodule too small for other assays  No frozen done  Discussed with surgeon  Section Code  A B  nodule  C D  nodule  E F  margin  G J  margin  Resident  James Kirby  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST LEFT EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST  report_end , 0.
