Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Specimen Type  LEFT BREAST MASS Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  HANNA Y IRIE M D  CASE  BS 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PATIENT  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME Resident  Michael W Bennett  M B   B C H   Jian Shen  M D   Ph D  Pathologist  Susan Lester  M D   Ph D  PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS  CONSULT SLIDES FROM ST ELIZABETH S MEDICAL CENTER  BOSTON  MA LEFT BREAST  EXCISION  96 3702  REMOVED_DATE    Atypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread associated with atypical apocrine adenosis  blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   No necrosis or calcifications are seen  Calcifications are associated with benign epithelium  Note  In 2 of 23 blocks there is a small area of adenosis  0 3 cm  which is involved by apocrine cells and a population of cells best interpreted as ALH with pagetoid spread  These cells are immunoreactive for estrogen and progesterone receptors  outside immunoperoxidase studies reviewed   This area was originally diagnosed as DCIS  However  the cytologic and architectural features are considered insufficient for this diagnosis  The lesion excised in this biopsy is not stated  No gross lesions were identified  Clinical correlation is suggested to ensure that the biopsy was representative of the clinical lesion  CLINICAL DATA  History  Family history of breast cancer  Appt date  Was REMOVED_DATE  Clinical Diagnosis  None given  TISSUE SUBMITTED  Consult slides  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received from St Elizabeth s Medical Center  736 Cambridge St   Pathology Department  BOSTON  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  are thirty five  35  slides  Thirty five  35  stained slides are labeled  96 3702  and sublabeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOV