Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Amend Addenda Type  Surgical Pathology Specimen Type  Consult material Procedure Date  Ordering Provider  CAPRICE CHRISTIAN GREENBERG M D  CASE  BS 08 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PATIENT  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME            Addended Report             Resident  Mariana A  Stoleru  M D  Pathologist  Deborah A Dillon  M D  PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS  CONSULT SLIDES FROM PATHOLOGY SERVICES INC   CAMBRIDGE  MA  RIGHT BREAST  INCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_DATE    INVASIVE CARCINOMA measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in this limited specimen  see note   No lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen  No definite carcinoma in situ is present in this limited specimen  Margins cannot be evaluated  see note   Scant normal mammary epithelium is present  NOTE  By report  the patient has a remote history of prostatic carcinoma and a history of melanoma diagnosed in 1994  Immunohistochemistry for prostate markers PRSA and PRAP is negative  Immunohistochemistry for melanoma markers REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is negative  Morphologic evaluation is severely limited by extensive crush artifact  On immunohistochemical studies  the tumor cells are positive for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and E cadherin and negative for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  The histologic appearance in minute well preserved areas coupled with the immunophenotype support a diagnosis of primary invasive ductal carcinoma of breast  Evaluation of tumor size is difficult due to specimen fragmentation  Correlation with imaging studies is suggested for best determination of tumor size  The specimen appears to have been received as unoriented tissue fragments  thus  margins cannot be evaluated  CLINICAL DATA  History  None given Clinical Diagnosis  IDLC TISSUE SUBMITTED  Consult slides  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received from Pathology Services  Inc   Pathology Department  640 Memorial Drive  Cambridge  MA REMOVED_CASE_ID  are two  32  glass slides  30 slides are unstained   The slides are labeled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and sublabeled  1    1 unstained  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    2  and  2 unstained  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   corresponding to a right breast  skin  biopsy  2 0 cm  performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient s name  By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated  of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es  related thereto  Final Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE  SURGICAL ADDENDUM  9 27 08   Immunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the following results for invasive carcinoma  outside block 2   Estrogen receptor POSITIVE Progesterone receptor POSITIVE   LOW REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu  c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  NEGATIVE  0  Hormone receptor analysis  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the invasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows  positive  10  of nuclei immunoreactive positive   low   0      10  of nuclei immunoreactive negative 0  of nuclei immunoreactive The lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet been determined  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu analysis  Negative  0   No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells  Negative  1    Faint weak immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells but only a portion of the membrane is positive  Positive  2   Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells  Positive  3   Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in  30  of tumor cells  Cytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result  External controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity  Some of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational use only  Addendum  1 by Deborah A Dillon M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE   report_end , 1.
