Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status  Signed Type  Surgical Pathology Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  DIAGNOSIS  A  Right breast  excision  Ductal carcinoma in situ  grade REMOVED_DATE  cribriform type  with microcalcifications  extensive and admixed with atypical ductal hyperplasia  see note   Fibrocystic changes with ductal hyperplasia and intraductal papillomas  B  Posterior margin of right breast  excision  Focal ductal carcinoma in situ  grade REMOVED_DATE  cribriform type  Fibrocystic changes with ductal hyperplasia  NOTE  In the right breast excision  specimen A   ductal carcinoma in situ and atypical ductal hyperplasia are present in multiple microscopic foci throughout the specimen  as well as in two nodular areas near the localizing wires and each associated with areas of fibroplasia and chronic inflammation consistent with two prior needle biopsy sites  the report of the Massachusetts General Hospital slide review  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is noted   Ductal carcinoma in situ and atypical ductal hyperplasia are present less than 1 mm  from inked margins in multiple foci including superior  lateral  medial and superficial margins  Ductal carcinoma in situ present in the posterior margin excision  specimen B  is greater than 4 mm  from the inked margin  Final Diagnosis by  Daniel D  Koelliker  M D  Clinical diagnosis   history  Right breast ductal carcinoma in situ and atypical ductal hyperplasia Tissue Designation  A Breast  excision with margins   right  long lateral  short inferior B Breast  excision with margins   right  posterior margin  suture furthest from margin Gross description  The specimen is received in formalin in two containers  Specimen A labeled  right breast  long lateral  short inferior  consists of a 6 3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  portion of fibroadipose tissue containing two localizing wires and marked with two separate sutures  and accompanied by a specimen X ray  The margins throughout are inked black  The sutures are designated as long lateral  short inferior on the requisition  based on these orientations the deep surface is identified and is inked red  The lateral half is double inked blue  The specimen is cross sectioned from superior towards inferior  Located in the superior portion a bent wire transverses the specimen from superficial to deep  In this area  there is a ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE  cm  hard  pink tan mass  Within this  there is a small metallic clip present  Adjacent to this  there is extensive fat necrosis and hemorrhage in the otherwise yellow  lobulated adipose tissue  More inferiorly  there is a second wire which extends from superficial to deep  Within this area near the wire  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  similar  hard  pink tan mass with surrounding fat necrosis  The entire specimen is submitted serially in fourteen equal cross sections from superior to inferior with most having subdesignations A for superficial and B for deep in a total of twenty five cassettes  The superior mass is entirely submitted in cross sections  5  where the wire was and  6  where the clip was  The inferior nodule is submitted in cross section  10 12  25 agg  all  Specimen B labeled  right breast posterior margin  suture furthest from margin  consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  portion of fibroadipose tissue with a suture on one surface which is inked black  The specimen is cross sectioned and serially submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  6 agg  all  Dictated by  DDK____ signature on file ____MICHAEL J  ROSS  M D  REMOVED_DATE   Final  ____ signature on file ____DANIEL D  KOELLIKER  M D  REMOVED_DATE   Final   report_end , 0.
