Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ACCESSIONED ON  14 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 42 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided      REVISED REPORT     Revision  1  Reason for Revision  ADDITIONAL OUTSIDE MATERIAL RECEIVED Revised by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Revised on 21 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 47 Revision  2  Reason for Revision  ADDITIONAL OUTSIDE MATERIAL RECEIVED Revised by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Revised on 28 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 51                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  This tumor appears slightly different from the carcinoma resected from the patient s left breast in 1985  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Edited by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 AUG 98 at 15 55                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 AUG 98 at 15 55                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTSIDE LOCATION REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  OUTSIDE INSTITUTION  RHODE ISLAND HOSPITAL OUTSIDE PATHOLOGIST  Monique DePaepe  M D  RHODE ISLAND HOSPITAL 593 EDDY STREET PROVIDENCE  RI REMOVED_CASE_ID OUTSIDE CLINICIAN  BANICE WEBBER  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT CORE    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BIOPSY  Date of Procedure  02 JUL 1998 Slides  5 Blocks  1  report_end , 1.
