Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  04 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  04 AUG 98 at 16 05 CLINICAL DATA  Right lump in 1979 treated with radiation  now new thickening and retraction right breast   Recurrence malignancy  sarcoma  or radiation fibrosis                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY  INFILTRATING MAMMARY CARCINOMA  Note  The biopsy shows fibrotic and adipose tissue with atypical epithelial appearing cells infiltrating as single cells and small single file like clusters  Immunohistochemical stains demonstrate that the atypical cells express keratin  Stains for smooth muscle actin  vimentin  and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID are negative  These results support the diagnosis of infiltrating carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Joseph Misdraji  MD Signed On  07 AUG 98 at 19 13 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Jacqueline Haas  MD                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 37 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin  labeled with the patient s name and unit number  and  right breast biopsy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of soft tan cores of tissue which are submitted in toto in cassette A  Gross Description by  Joe Serra Resident  SELIM NASSER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Robin Schoenthaler  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   CORE BIOPSY, 0.
