Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 91 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 91 at 16 11 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass  known previous lymphoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT BREAST BIOPSY   INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  EXTENDING INTO DUCTS  ATYPICAL INTRADUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  The tumor measures REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest diameter and extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest inked margin  Greater than 90  of the tumor is infiltrating  Diagnosis by  Eugene Jerome Mark  M D  Signed On  24 REMOVED_MONTH 91 at 13 10 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                      IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  the results of prospective staining of 100 breast tumors were compared with determinations of estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  93  of tumors that reacted with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  100  of tumors that failed to stain were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 91 at 11 21     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  BIOPSY   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   1   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean REMOVED_DATE   and median of 3  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistently shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 91 at 17 34     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726 8865  estrogen receptor  51 fm mg cytosolic protein progesterone receptor  107 fm mg cytosolic protein Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received on ice  labeled  Left breast mass   is a 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 3 cm piece of breast tissue  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1 cm  gritty  ill defined nodule approaching to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the nearest margin  A representative section is frozen as Frozen Section  1 and saved frozen  Tissue is submitted for Estrogen receptors and BRDU studies  The remainder of the tissue is submitted in A through K  Resident  Robert F  Cheek  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  Elizabeth Bailey  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO  Steven Ralph Levisohn  M D  David William Rattner  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS BIOPSY, 0.
