ompanying radiograph demonstrates two encircled foci of microcalcifications  one at the hookwire tip  and one remote from the tip at one end of the specimen  The specimen is sectioned  revealing abundant dense tan white fibrous tissue occupying one half of the specimen  half with calcifications   The remaining half is mostly soft  lobulated tan yellow adipose tissue  without definitive masses  lesions or other abnormalities grossly  The entire specimen is serially sectioned and sequentially submitted  with perpendicular ends in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and small focus of calcification  remote from hookwire tip  likely in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Area of interest per hookwire tip in micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Entire specimen  sequentially  multi frags  ESS  Part B    2  Additional right breast tissue  deep   and consists of an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue without masses  lesions or other abnormalities noted grossly upon sectioning  The entire specimen is submitted  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  7 frags total  ESS  Part C    3  Mole  right breast   consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  depth  unoriented tan white skin ellipse  with an eccentric REMOVED_DATE cm ill defined pigmented lesion less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest long axis margin and less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest tip  The specimen is inked and sectioned  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Tips  2 frags  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Body  3 frags  ESS  CASE NUMBER  REMOVED_CASE_ID  db ag By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated  of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es  related thereto  Final Diagnosis by Kirstine Yung Ting Oh M D   Electronically signed on 12 11 2007  report_end , 0.
