 were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the following results for invasive carcinoma  block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Estrogen receptor NEGATIVE Progesterone receptor NEGATIVE REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu  c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  POSITIVE  2    HETEROGENEOUS  Cytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID POSITIVE TTF 1 NEGATIVE Note  The tumor cells are positive for the cytokeratin marker REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and are negative for TTF 1  This pattern is consistent with  but not specific for  breast carcinoma  Normal epithelial cells are not present to serve as an internal control for ER and PR  Repeat studies on the excision should be considered  The carcinoma demonstrates cytoplasmic immunoreactivity for ER  which is considered a negative result  The block has been sent for FISH studies for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu amplification  Interpretation  Hormone receptor analysis  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows  positive  10  of nuclei immunoreactive positive   low  0  to  10  of nuclei immunoreactive negative 0  nuclei immunoreactive The lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet been determined  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu analysis  Negative  0   No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells  Negative  1    Faint weak immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells but only a portion of the membrane is positive  Positive  2    Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells  Positive  3    Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells  Cytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result  Some of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational use only  Addendum  1 by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE  SURGICAL ADDENDUM  FISH was performed by USLABS using the PathVysion HER 2 DNA Probe Kit with the following results  block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Result  NOT AMPLIFIED The Her 2 cen 17 ratio   REMOVED_DATE  The average of Her 2 neu copies per cell  REMOVED_DATE  The average of cen 17 copies per cell  REMOVED_DATE  The cutoff point for assessing HER 2 neu gene amplification is a ratio of REMOVED_DATE  Addendum  2 by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE   report_end , 1.
