Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Amend Addenda Type  Surgical Pathology Specimen Type  Breast core needle biopsy Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  JULIE ANN RITNER M D  CASE  BS 09 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PATIENT  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME            Addended Report             Resident  George Lin  M D   Ph D  Pathologist  Susan Lester  M D   Ph D  PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  UPPER OUTER  14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A REMOVED_DATE  CM PALPABLE CYSTIC CIRCUMSCRIBED MASS WITH BRANCHING DYSTROPHIC AND PLEOMORPHIC CALCIFICATIONS  INVASIVE ADENOCARCINOMA  poorly differentiated  with apocrine features  measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size  see note   An immunoperoxidase study for p63 and cytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID confirms the absence of myoepithelial cells in the areas of invasion  No lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen  No carcinoma in situ is seen in this limited specimen  Prominent heterotopic bone formation is present  Immunoperoxidase studies are performed with the following results for invasive carcinoma  Estrogen receptor POSITIVE Progesterone receptor POSITIVE   LOW REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu POSITIVE  3   Cytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID POSITIVE Cytokeratin 14 POSITIVE Cytokeratin  PANK  POSITIVE Note  The carcinoma has a very unusual histologic appearance  The carcinoma invades as large circumscribed nests of cells with a micropapillary or cribriform pattern  Necrosis is present  Bone formation is present  but the associated osteocytes and reactive stroma appear to be benign  The stromal cells are not immunoreactive for cytokeratin  The block will be sent for FISH analysis for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu amplification  CLINICAL DATA  HISTORY  Large palpable complex cystic mass   very hemorrhagic  Malignant cells were present on FNA  Differential diagnosis  primary breast cancer vs other malignancy  Time in formalin   2 pm  BREAST IMAGING FINDING  1  Left  REMOVED_DATE cm  palpable  circumscribed  complex cystic mass  LOCATION  1  Left  upper outer  TYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY  1  14 G Ultrasound  TISSUE SUBMITTED  A 1  Left breast core biopsy in one orange cassette  GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received in formalin  in one part  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  orange left breast   and consists of an orange cassette  which contains multiple tan pink fibrofatty cores  1 8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate   which are submitted in toto  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Tissue received in orange cassette  multi frags  ESS  Immunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following criteria  Hormone receptor analysis  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the carcinoma is reported as follows  positive  10  of nuclei immunoreactive positive   low  0  to  10  of nuclei immunoreactive negative 0  nuclei immunoreactive The lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet been determined  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu analysis  Negative  0   No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells  Negative  1    Faint weak immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells but only a portion of the membrane is positive  Equivocal  2    Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells or moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells  Positive  3    Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   30  of tumor cells  Cytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result  External controls are evaluated and show appropriate immunoreactivity  The immunoperoxidase  immunofluorescence and in situ hybridization tests performed at Brigham and Women s Hospital were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the Department of Pathology at BWH  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  lmc lp CASE NUMBER  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated  of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es  related thereto  Final Diagnosis by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 18  2009 at 05 19 40PM SURGICAL ADDENDUM   9 28 09  FISH was performed by Clarient using the PathVysion HER 2 DNA Probe Kit with the following  block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Results  AMPLIFIED HER 2 CEP 17 ratio   REMOVED_DATE  The average of HER 2 copies per cell  REMOVED_DATE  The average centromere 17 copies per cell  REMOVED_DATE  REFERENCE RANGE  NOT AMPLIFIED HER 2 CEP 17 ratio   REMOVED_DATE  EQUIVOCAL HER 2 CEP 17 ratio REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE  AMPLIFIED REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID CEP 17 ratio   REMOVED_DATE  Addendum  1 by Andrea L Richardson M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 28  2009 at 05 33 55PM  report_end , 1.
