 an unremarkable yellow tan cut surface  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  nodular tissue serially sectioned  multiple frags  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  skin serially sectioned  multiple frags  ESS  lmb lp By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated  of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es  related thereto  Resident Review by Peter M Sadow M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE  Prelim Dx Release by Peter M Sadow M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE  No Action   Prelim Sent by Peter M Sadow M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE  Final Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M D   Electronically signed on 2 8 2006 SURGICAL ADDENDUM  The carcinoma is in an area of breast tissue  i e  ducts and lobules are present in the adjacent tissue  and does not involve the overlying skin  There is extensive tumor necrosis    1 HPF   No carcinoma in situ is present  There is no lymphovascular invasion  By imaging studies  the carcinoma is in a different area of the breast than was her prior breast carcinoma  The carcinoma is extensively present at the unoriented margin  Immunoperoxidase studies were performed at BWH and FISH was performed by USLABS  PathVysion HER 2 DNA Probe Kit  with the following results for invasive carcinoma  block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Estrogen receptor NEGATIVE Progesterone receptor NEGATIVE REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu  IHC  WEAKLY POSITIVE  2   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu  FISH  AMPLIFIED  4 4 2 2   REMOVED_DATE   Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen and progesterone receptors  The patient s prior breast cancer in 2000  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the carcinoma in her lung in 2001  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  are compared to the current carcinoma  All three are poorly differentiated carcinomas and are essentially identical in appearance  All three carcinomas are negative for ER and PR  The prior breast carcinoma was negative for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu  0   The carcinoma in the lung was not tested for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu  The prior breast carcinoma was not associated with lymphovascular invasion and her lymph nodes were negative  The location of the current carcinoma in the breast at a site away from the original breast carcinoma  the absence of associated lymphovascular invasion  and the presence of a low level of REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu  all suggest that this carcinoma is likely a new primary carcinoma  However  an intramammary metastasis cannot be completely excluded  Addendum by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE  Addendum  1 by Susan Lester M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE   report_end , 0.
