rely fibrous tissue  whereas the remaining 60  of the specimen is a mix of roughly 60  adipose and 40  fibrous tissue  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  superior portion of specimen with clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  1 frag in each  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  anterior  posterior and medial margins with fibrous tissue  1 frag  RSS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  inferior margin  1 frag in each  RSS   NOTE  approximately 50  of the specimen and 75  of the fibrous tissue is submitted   Part B  labeled   2   additional left breast tissue  and consists of one fragment of breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm  Half of the surface is inked in black  and the other half is inked in yellow by the surgeon  A biopsy site with gel foam is identified in the central portion of the specimen abutting the black inked margin  The gel foam comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the yellow inked margin  The remainder of the cut surface consists entirely of yellow adipose tissue  The biopsy site cavity is submitted in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  additional left breast tissue  1 frag in each  RSS   NOTE  approximately 60  of the specimen and 100  of the fibrous tissue have been submitted   ESN lp By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated  of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es  related thereto  Final Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on 5 16 2006  report_end , 0.
