Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Specimen Type  Breast  excisional tissue Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  JULIE L JONES M D  CASE  BS 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PATIENT  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME Resident  Stephanie Schulte  M D  Pathologist  Susan Lester  M D   Ph D  PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST  EXCISION FOR A PALPABLE MASS  PHYLLODES TUMOR  low grade  4 4 cm   see note  The stroma is moderately cellular with mild nuclear pleomorphism  Moderate stromal overgrowth is present  Mitoses number up to three per ten  3 10  high power fields  No necrosis or hemorrhage is present  The borders are circumscribed  without invasion into the adjacent stroma  No heterologous elements are present  The tumor is present at the cauterized anterior resection margin and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior  medial  lateral  superior  and inferior margins  Note  Phyllodes tumors are very rare in women under the age of 20  The mitotic rate  stromal cellularity  and focal stromal overgrowth favor classification of this lesion as a phyllodes tumor  rather than a cellular fibroadenoma  CLINICAL DATA  History  A 14 year old female with left breast fibroepithelial low grade tumor versus fibroadenoma  Operation  Left breast excisional biopsy  Operative Findings  None given  Clinical Diagnosis  Left breast mass  TISSUE SUBMITTED  A 1  Left breast mass  GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received fresh  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and   1  Left breast mass long lateral short superior   and consists of a tan yellow portion of fibrofatty soft tissue  4 5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  that has a short suture marking superior and a long suture marking lateral  The specimen is inked  The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins  posterior black  anterior blue  superior red  inferior green  lateral yellow  medial orange   and sectioned from medial to lateral  Sectioning shows a well 