Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  LESTER  SUSAN  M D  PH D  DIAGNOSIS  by LESTER SUSAN M D  PH D  LEFT BREAST  WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS  Sclerosing adenosis with hyalinized stroma  Focal epithelial hyperplasia  Biopsy site changes  Note  A discrete mass forming lesion is not seen  There are multiple areas of sclerosing adenosis associated with dense stroma which may correlate with the radiologic mass  Compared with the prior core needle biopsy  the nuclear changes are much less pronounced  In this setting  it is likely the nuclear changes were related either to the prior therapy or to reactive inflammatory changes after a prior attempted cyst aspiration  No malignancy is seen after complete histologic examination of the specimen  including margins  CLINICAL DATA  History  53 year old woman with a history of right breast well differentiated invasive carcinoma with LVI and negative lymph nodes  ER PR positive  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu negative  Now with a left breast circumscribed mass at 2 00  A core biopsy on REMOVED_DATE  showed sclerosing adenosis with nuclear atypia  Operation  Left breast wire localized excisional biopsy  TISSUE SUBMITTED  1  Left breast tissue  short stitch superior  long stitch lateral  whipstitch at deep margin  RADIOGRAPHIC REPORT  Mass in specimen  only by ultrasound   Dr  D  Smith GROSS DESCRIPTION  by CHEN JEY HSIN M D  PH D  The specimen is received fresh  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast tissue  short stitch superior  long stitch lateral  whipstitch deep margin   and consists of fibroadipose tissue  4 5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm   oriented by a short stitch marking the superior surface  long stitch marking the lateral surface  and a whipstitch marking the deep surface  In place is a wire  which enters the specimen at the supralateral anterior surface  directed medially into the specimen  An accompanying specimen radiograph reveals dense tissue throughout the specimen without a discrete mass  The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins  posterior black  anterior blue  superior red  inferior green  lateral yellow  medial orange  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral  revealing yellow tan  rubbery breast tissue  involving approximately 90  of the specimen and extending to all surgical resection margins  Within the specimen is a focal area of yellow tan tissue  0 3 cm in diameter   grossly consistent with fat necrosis  extending to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior surface  The specimen is entirely submitted for microscopic examination from medial to lateral  Micro REMOVED_DATE  Medial margin  perpendicular  3 frags  ESS  Micro REMOVED_DATE  Serial sections from medial to lateral  6 frags  ESS  Micro REMOVED_DATE  Lateral margin  perpendicular  3 frags  ESS  jhc Reports to  RHEI  ESTHER M D  SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST   EXCISIONAL TISSUE W MARGINS  report_end , 0.
