Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status  Signed Type  Surgical Pathology Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  ADDENDUM REPORT Addendum  1 Entered  REMOVED_DATE  1508 E E      ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION     This report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing additional diagnostic information  The original diagnosis is unchanged  Immunohistochemical staining on the formalin fixed  paraffin embedded block reveals these results for the ductal carcinoma in situ  Estrogen receptor  POSITIVE   10  of nuclei stained  Estrogen receptor  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and or progesterone receptor  PgR 1REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  is assessed visually by quantitation of the percent of tumor cells staining  Total fixation time is 32 hours  Addeundum Signed Electronically Signed COVELL LINDA M D  REMOVED_DATE  DIAGNOSIS  Left breast  needle biopsy  Ductal carcinoma in situ  cribriform pattern  with low grade nuclei  2 mm  focus in one core  with rare microcalcifications  microcalcifications also present in lumens of bordering non neoplastic ductules  NOTE  Results of estrogen receptor immunohistochemistry will be reported in an addendum  Final Diagnosis  Linda M  Covell  M D  Clinical diagnosis   history  Strong family history of breast cancer  4 mm  hypoechoic mass  2 o clock left breast  cancer  versus lymph node Tissue Designation  Breast  needle biopsy   left Gross description  The specimen is received in formalin in one container  labeled  guided breast biopsy  left breast  and consists of three soft  yellowish white  glistening needle biopsies ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE cm  in length x REMOVED_DATE cm  in diameter to 1 6 cm  in length x REMOVED_DATE cm  in diameter  The specimens are marked with black ink  3X all  Total fixation time is 32 hours  Dictated by  LV____ signature on file ____RICHARD SAMPSON  M D  REMOVED_DATE   Final  ____ signature on file ____ REMOVED_DATE   Final   report_end , 1.
Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  31 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  31 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11 44 CLINICAL DATA  Question invasive carcinoma  Margins please                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  50   SEE NOTE   INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  50    FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CYST FORMATION AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS   MICROCALCIFICATIONS  BREAST  RIGHT  ADDITIONAL LATERAL AND POSTERIOR MARGINS   EXCISION  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The tumor measures REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest diameter  It involves the deep margin  The specimen designated   additional lateral and posterior margins   is involved with infiltrating ductal carcinoma  10   and intraductal carcinoma  90   on one edge  but it does not extend through the specimen  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   EXCISION  FIFTEEN LYMPH NODES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  LEVEL II   EXCISION  TWO LYMPH NODES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 16                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm piece of breast tissue with an attached ellipse of skin which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  There is a short silk suture at the superior margin and a long silk suture at the lateral margin  The specimen is inked  anterior designated yellow  and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm poorly defined  white  firm  gritty area which involves the deep margin and comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin  A representative section of the deep resection margin is frozen as FS 1 and saved frozen  A representative section of the inferior resection margin is frozen as FS 3  now A  Representative serial sections from lateral to medial are submitted in B through H  with B through E being the lateral half and the remainder being the medial half  Labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  right breast additional lateral and posterior margins   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm piece of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal fibrous tissue with multiple cysts up to REMOVED_DATE cm  Submitted entirely in I through S  Labeled  right axilla nodes   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm piece of fatty tissue  from which multiple tan  rubbery lymph nodes  ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm are dissected  portions of these lymph nodes are submitted in T through V  Labeled  Level II   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm piece of fatty tissue  from which two lymph nodes  each REMOVED_DATE cm  is dissected  The nodes are submitted in W  and the remainder in X  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1 2  BREAST RIGHT  BIOPSY  INFILTRATING   INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  SOME IS COMEDO  TYPE   CARCINOMA APPROACHES TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF DEEP MARGIN  O R  Resident  RICHARD S  HAMILTON  HMS O R  Diagnosis by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  RIGHT BREAST TISSUE PART B  ADDITIONAL LATERAL   POSTERIOR MARGINS  RIGHT BREA PART C  AXILLA NODES  RIGHT  PART D  LEVEL II, 1.
